{"task_id": "Mbpp/4", "solution": "```python\ndef heap_queue_largest(numbers: list[int], n: int) -> list[int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the n largest integers from a list of numbers, returning them in descending order.\n    A manual min-heap maintains the n largest elements found so far.\n    \"\"\"\n    min_heap = []\n\n    # Helper functions for min-heap operations, defined inline.\n    def _sift_up(heap_list, idx):\n        parent_idx = (idx - 1) // 2\n        while idx > 0 and heap_list[idx] < heap_list[parent_idx]:\n            heap_list[idx], heap_list[parent_idx] = heap_list[parent_idx], heap_list[idx]\n            idx = parent_idx\n            parent_idx = (idx - 1) // 2\n\n    def _sift_down(heap_list, idx):\n        size = len(heap_list)\n        while True:\n            left_child_idx = 2 * idx + 1\n            right_child_idx = 2 * idx + 2\n            smallest_idx = idx\n\n            if left_child_idx < size and heap_list[left_child_idx] < heap_list[smallest_idx]:\n                smallest_idx = left_child_idx\n            if right_child_idx < size and heap_list[right_child_idx] < heap_list[smallest_idx]:\n                smallest_idx = right_child_idx\n\n            if smallest_idx != idx:\n                heap_list[idx], heap_list[smallest_idx] = heap_list[smallest_idx], heap_list[idx]\n                idx = smallest_idx\n            else:\n                break\n\n    def _heappush(heap_list, item):\n        heap_list.append(item)\n        _sift_up(heap_list, len(heap_list) - 1)\n\n    def _heappop(heap_list):\n        if not heap_list:\n            return None\n        if len(heap_list) == 1:\n            return heap_list.pop()\n\n        root_item = heap_list[0]\n        heap_list[0] = heap_list.pop()\n        _sift_down(heap_list, 0)\n        return root_item\n\n    # Process numbers to find the n largest using the min-heap\n    for num in numbers:\n        if len(min_heap) < n:\n            _heappush(min_heap, num)\n        elif n > 0 and num > min_heap[0]:\n            _heappop(min_heap)\n            _heappush(min_heap, num)\n\n    # Extract elements from the heap and sort them in descending order.\n    # Popping from a min-heap gives elements in ascending order.\n    result = []\n    while min_heap:\n        result.append(_heappop(min_heap))\n\n    # Reverse the list to achieve descending order.\n    result.reverse()\n    return result\n```"}
