{"task_id": "Mbpp/11", "solution": "def remove_Occ(input_string: str, target_char: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Removes the first and last occurrences of a specified character from a string.\n    Handles cases where the character appears once or not at all.\n    \"\"\"\n    first_idx = input_string.find(target_char)\n    last_idx = input_string.rfind(target_char)\n\n    if first_idx == -1:\n        # Character not found, return original string.\n        return input_string\n    elif first_idx == last_idx:\n        # Character found only once, remove that single occurrence.\n        return input_string[:first_idx] + input_string[first_idx + 1:]\n    else:\n        # Character found multiple times, remove last then first.\n        # Removing last first preserves the index of the first occurrence.\n        temp_string = input_string[:last_idx] + input_string[last_idx + 1:]\n        return temp_string[:first_idx] + temp_string[first_idx + 1:]"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/11", "solution": "def remove_Occ(input_string: str, char_to_remove: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Removes the first and last occurrences of a specified character from a string.\n    Handles cases where the character appears once or not at all by removing the single occurrence or making no changes.\"\"\"\n\n    first_idx = input_string.find(char_to_remove)\n\n    if first_idx == -1:\n        # Character not found, return the original string\n        return input_string\n\n    last_idx = input_string.rfind(char_to_remove)\n\n    if first_idx == last_idx:\n        # Character found exactly once\n        return input_string[:first_idx] + input_string[first_idx+1:]\n    else:\n        # Character found two or more times, remove first and last\n        return input_string[:first_idx] + input_string[first_idx+1:last_idx] + input_string[last_idx+1:]"}
