{"task_id": "Mbpp/57", "solution": "```python\ndef find_Max_Num(listOfDigits: list[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Forms the largest possible integer from a list of digits.\n    It sorts digits as strings using a custom comparison logic.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not listOfDigits:\n        return 0\n\n    str_digits = [str(d) for d in listOfDigits]\n\n    # Custom comparison function: returns <0 if x should precede y, >0 otherwise.\n    def _compare_xy_for_sort(x: str, y: str) -> int:\n        return int(y + x) - int(x + y)\n\n    # Wrapper for list.sort(key=...) to use a 3-way comparison function.\n    class _CmpKeyWrapper:\n        def __init__(self, obj):\n            self.obj = obj\n        def __lt__(self, other):\n            return _compare_xy_for_sort(self.obj, other.obj) < 0\n        def __eq__(self, other):\n            return _compare_xy_for_sort(self.obj, other.obj) == 0\n        def __hash__(self):\n            return hash(self.obj)\n\n    str_digits.sort(key=_CmpKeyWrapper)\n\n    result_str = \"\".join(str_digits)\n\n    # Handle cases like [0, 0, 0] which should return 0, not '000' -> 0\n    if result_str and int(result_str) == 0:\n        return 0\n\n    return int(result_str)\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/12", "solution": "```python\ndef _calculate_row_sum(row: list) -> float:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the sum of elements in a single row.\"\"\"\n    return sum(row)\n\ndef sort_matrix(matrix: list[list]) -> list[list]:\n    \"\"\"Sorts the rows of a matrix by their sums in ascending order.\"\"\"\n    row_sum_pairs = []\n    for row in matrix:\n        row_sum = _calculate_row_sum(row)\n        row_sum_pairs.append((row_sum, row))\n\n    row_sum_pairs.sort(key=lambda item: item[0])\n\n    sorted_matrix = [pair[1] for pair in row_sum_pairs]\n    return sorted_matrix\n```"}
