{"task_id": "Mbpp/68", "solution": "```python\ndef is_Monotonic(arr):\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if an array is monotonic (either non-decreasing or non-increasing).\n    Handles empty and single-element arrays as True.\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(arr) <= 1:\n        return True\n\n    is_non_decreasing = True\n    is_non_increasing = True\n\n    for i in range(len(arr) - 1):\n        if arr[i] > arr[i+1]:\n            is_non_decreasing = False\n        if arr[i] < arr[i+1]:\n            is_non_increasing = False\n\n        # If both flags are false, the array is neither, so we can exit early.\n        if not is_non_decreasing and not is_non_increasing:\n            return False\n\n    return is_non_decreasing or is_non_increasing\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/67", "solution": "```python\ndef bell_number(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the nth Bell number using the Aitken's array (Bell triangle) method.\n    This method iteratively computes the values, where B(n) is the first element of row n.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 1\n\n    # current_row stores the elements of the current row in the Bell triangle.\n    # B(n) will be the first element of current_row after n iterations.\n    current_row = [0] * (n + 1)\n    current_row[0] = 1  # A[0][0] = B(0) = 1\n\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        next_row = [0] * (n + 1)\n        next_row[0] = current_row[i - 1]  # The first element of new row is the last of the previous.\n        for j in range(1, i + 1):\n            next_row[j] = next_row[j - 1] + current_row[j - 1]  # A[i][j] = A[i][j-1] + A[i-1][j-1]\n        current_row = next_row  # Update current_row to the newly calculated row\n\n    return current_row[0]\n```"}
