{"task_id": "Mbpp/74", "solution": "```python\ndef is_samepatterns(string_list: list[str], pattern_list: list[str]) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if a list of strings follows a pattern sequence with a consistent one-to-one mapping.\n    Both lists must have equal length for a successful match.\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(string_list) != len(pattern_list):\n        return False\n\n    string_to_pattern_map = {}\n    pattern_to_string_map = {}\n\n    for s, p in zip(string_list, pattern_list):\n        # Check string-to-pattern consistency\n        if s in string_to_pattern_map:\n            if string_to_pattern_map[s] != p:\n                return False\n\n        # Check pattern-to-string consistency\n        if p in pattern_to_string_map:\n            if pattern_to_string_map[p] != s:\n                return False\n\n        # Update mappings if consistent or new\n        string_to_pattern_map[s] = p\n        pattern_to_string_map[p] = s\n\n    return True\n```"}
