{"task_id": "Mbpp/75", "solution": "```python\ndef find_tuples(list_of_tuples: list[tuple[int, ...]], k: int) -> list[tuple[int, ...]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Filters a list of tuples, returning only those where all elements are divisible by k.\n    It returns a list of tuples where each tuple from the input has all its elements divisible by k.\n    \"\"\"\n    result_tuples = []\n    for current_tuple in list_of_tuples:\n        all_elements_divisible = True\n        for element in current_tuple:\n            if k == 0:\n                # If k is 0, division by zero is problematic.\n                # In general, no number is divisible by 0 except 0 itself,\n                # and 0 % 0 is often considered an error or undefined.\n                # For this problem, if k is 0, we can assume no elements are divisible by k\n                # unless a specific behavior for 0%0 is defined.\n                # Given the context of \"divisible by k\", if k is 0, it's generally false.\n                all_elements_divisible = False\n                break\n            if element % k != 0:\n                all_elements_divisible = False\n                break\n        if all_elements_divisible:\n            result_tuples.append(current_tuple)\n    return result_tuples\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/74", "solution": "```python\ndef is_samepatterns(sequence: list[str], patterns: list[str]) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if a sequence follows a pattern with a consistent one-to-one mapping.\n    Returns True if the mapping is consistent and lengths are equal, False otherwise.\"\"\"\n    if len(sequence) != len(patterns):\n        return False\n\n    seq_to_pat_map = {}\n    pat_to_seq_map = {}\n\n    for i in range(len(sequence)):\n        s_char = sequence[i]\n        p_char = patterns[i]\n\n        if s_char in seq_to_pat_map:\n            if seq_to_pat_map[s_char] != p_char:\n                return False\n        else:\n            seq_to_pat_map[s_char] = p_char\n\n        if p_char in pat_to_seq_map:\n            if pat_to_seq_map[p_char] != s_char:\n                return False\n        else:\n            pat_to_seq_map[p_char] = s_char\n\n    return True\n```\n"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/75", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List, Tuple\n\ndef find_tuples(list_of_tuples: List[Tuple[int, ...]], k: int) -> List[Tuple[int, ...]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Filters a list of tuples, returning a new list containing only tuples\n    where all elements are divisible by k.\n    This function operates on integer tuples and an integer divisor k.\n    \"\"\"\n    return [\n        current_tuple for current_tuple in list_of_tuples\n        if all(element % k == 0 for element in current_tuple)\n    ]\n```"}
