{"task_id": "Mbpp/71", "solution": "```python\ndef comb_sort(arr: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"Sorts a list of elements using the Comb Sort algorithm.\"\"\"\n    arr_copy = arr[:]  # Create a mutable copy of the input list.\n    n = len(arr_copy)\n\n    gap = n\n    shrink_factor = 1.3\n    swapped = True  # Initialize to True to ensure the loop runs at least once.\n\n    while gap > 1 or swapped:\n        if gap > 1:\n            gap = int(gap / shrink_factor) # Shrink the gap.\n\n        swapped = False\n        # Perform a pass similar to bubble sort with the current gap.\n        for i in range(n - gap):\n            if arr_copy[i] > arr_copy[i + gap]:\n                arr_copy[i], arr_copy[i + gap] = arr_copy[i + gap], arr_copy[i]\n                swapped = True\n\n    return arr_copy\n```"}
