{"task_id": "Mbpp/100", "solution": "```python\ndef _is_palindrome(n: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if an integer is a palindrome by comparing its string representation with its reverse.\"\"\"\n    s = str(n)\n    return s == s[::-1]\n\ndef _find_next_palindrome_logic(start_num: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Iteratively searches for the next smallest palindrome strictly greater than start_num.\"\"\"\n    current_num = start_num + 1\n    while True:\n        if _is_palindrome(current_num):\n            return current_num\n        current_num += 1\n\ndef next_smallest_palindrome(input_integer: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Finds the next smallest palindrome strictly greater than the input integer.\"\"\"\n    return _find_next_palindrome_logic(input_integer)\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/99", "solution": "```python\ndef decimal_to_binary(decimal_num: int) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    Converts a decimal integer to its binary string representation.\n\n    The returned binary string will not contain leading zeros,\n    except for the number 0 itself, which is represented as '0'.\n    \"\"\"\n    if decimal_num == 0:\n        return '0'\n\n    binary_string = \"\"\n    temp_num = decimal_num\n    while temp_num > 0:\n        remainder = temp_num % 2\n        binary_string = str(remainder) + binary_string\n        temp_num //= 2\n\n    return binary_string\n```"}
