{"task_id": "Mbpp/101", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List, Any\n\ndef kth_element(array: List[Any], k: int) -> Any:\n    \"\"\"Finds the kth element in an array using 1-based indexing.\n    Raises ValueError for empty array or IndexError for k out of bounds.\n    \"\"\"\n    # First, check if the array is empty, raising ValueError if true.\n    if not array:\n        raise ValueError(\"Array cannot be empty\")\n\n    # Next, validate the k value, raising IndexError if it's out of bounds.\n    if k < 1 or k > len(array):\n        raise IndexError(\"k is out of bounds\")\n\n    # Translate the 1-based index k to a 0-based index.\n    zero_based_index = k - 1\n\n    # Access and return the element from the array using the 0-based index.\n    return array[zero_based_index]\n```"}
