{"task_id": "Mbpp/103", "solution": "```python\ndef _factorial(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the factorial of a non-negative integer.\n    This helper function computes n!.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 1\n    res = 1\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        res *= i\n    return res\n\ndef _combinations(n: int, k: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the binomial coefficient \"n choose k\".\n    This helper function computes n! / (k! * (n-k)!).\n    \"\"\"\n    if k < 0 or k > n:\n        return 0\n    if k == 0 or k == n:\n        return 1\n    if k > n // 2:\n        k = n - k\n\n    # Calculate using factorials or optimized multiplication/division\n    # For this context, direct factorial calculation is suitable given the constraints.\n    return _factorial(n) // (_factorial(k) * _factorial(n - k))\n\ndef eulerian_num(n: int, m: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Computes the Eulerian number a(n, m).\n    This function calculates the number of permutations of {1, ..., n} with m ascents.\n    \"\"\"\n    if m < 0 or m >= n:\n        return 0\n\n    eulerian_sum = 0\n    for k in range(m + 1):\n        term = ((-1)**k) * _combinations(n + 1, k) * ((m - k + 1)**n)\n        eulerian_sum += term\n\n    return eulerian_sum\n```"}
