{"task_id": "Mbpp/109", "solution": "```python\ndef odd_Equivalent(s: str, n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the count of odd numbers over n rotations of a binary string.\"\"\"\n    odd_count = 0\n    current_s = s\n\n    for _ in range(n):\n        # Check if the last character is '1' to determine oddness.\n        if current_s and current_s[-1] == '1':\n            odd_count += 1\n\n        # Rotate the string by moving the first character to the end.\n        if current_s:\n            current_s = current_s[1:] + current_s[0]\n\n    return odd_count\n```"}
