{"task_id": "Mbpp/113", "solution": "```python\ndef check_integer(input_string: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Determines if a given string represents a valid integer, handling spaces and signs.\n    This function does not use regular expressions.\n    \"\"\"\n    s = input_string.strip()\n\n    if not s:\n        return False\n\n    start_index = 0\n    if s[0] == '+' or s[0] == '-':\n        start_index = 1\n\n    # An empty string after handling a sign (e.g., \"+\", \"-\") is not a valid integer.\n    if start_index == len(s):\n        return False\n\n    for i in range(start_index, len(s)):\n        if not ('0' <= s[i] <= '9'): # Manually check if character is a digit\n            return False\n\n    return True\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/111", "solution": "```python\ndef common_in_nested_lists(list_of_lists: list[list]) -> list:\n    \"\"\"Finds elements common to all inner lists within a given list of lists.\n    Returns a list of these common elements, with order not guaranteed.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not list_of_lists:\n        return []\n\n    common_elements_set = set(list_of_lists[0])\n\n    for inner_list in list_of_lists[1:]:\n        common_elements_set = common_elements_set.intersection(set(inner_list))\n        if not common_elements_set:  # Optimization: if no common elements found, no need to check further\n            break\n\n    return list(common_elements_set)\n```"}
