{"task_id": "Mbpp/131", "solution": "```python\ndef _is_vowel(char: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if a given character is a vowel (a, e, i, o, u, case-insensitive, 'y' excluded).\"\"\"\n    return char.lower() in 'aeiou'\n\ndef reverse_vowels(s: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Reverses only the vowels in an input string, preserving non-vowel positions and cases.\"\"\"\n    char_list = list(s)\n    vowel_indices = []\n    collected_vowels = []\n\n    for i, char in enumerate(char_list):\n        if _is_vowel(char):\n            vowel_indices.append(i)\n            collected_vowels.append(char)\n\n    collected_vowels.reverse()\n\n    # Place the reversed vowels back into their original positions.\n    for i, vowel_idx in enumerate(vowel_indices):\n        char_list[vowel_idx] = collected_vowels[i]\n\n    return \"\".join(char_list)\n```"}
