{"task_id": "Mbpp/120", "solution": "```python\ndef max_product_tuple(list_of_tuples: list) -> float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the maximum absolute product from a list of two-number tuples.\n\n    Args:\n        list_of_tuples: A list where each element is expected to be a tuple\n                        containing exactly two numbers (integers or floats).\n\n    Returns:\n        A single number (float) representing the maximum absolute product found.\n        Returns 0.0 if the input list is empty or contains no valid tuples.\n\n    Raises:\n        TypeError: If the input is not a list.\n        ValueError: If a tuple does not contain exactly two numbers or\n                    if numbers are not numeric.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Implementation details\n    if not isinstance(list_of_tuples, list):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input must be a list.\")\n\n    if not list_of_tuples:\n        return 0.0\n\n    max_abs_product = 0.0\n    found_valid_tuple = False\n\n    for i, item in enumerate(list_of_tuples):\n        if not isinstance(item, tuple):\n            # As per FR3, invalid tuples are handled appropriately. Raising ValueError.\n            raise ValueError(f\"Element at index {i} is not a tuple: {item}\")\n\n        if len(item) != 2:\n            # As per FR3, invalid tuples are handled appropriately. Raising ValueError.\n            raise ValueError(f\"Tuple at index {i} must contain exactly two numbers, found {len(item)}: {item}\")\n\n        num1, num2 = item\n\n        if not isinstance(num1, (int, float)) or not isinstance(num2, (int, float)):\n            # As per FR3, invalid tuples are handled appropriately. Raising ValueError.\n            raise ValueError(f\"Elements in tuple at index {i} must be numbers, found: {item}\")\n\n        product = num1 * num2\n        abs_product = abs(product)\n\n        if not found_valid_tuple or abs_product > max_abs_product:\n            max_abs_product = abs_product\n            found_valid_tuple = True\n\n    if not found_valid_tuple:\n        # If the list contained only invalid tuples after filtering\n        return 0.0\n\n    return max_abs_product\n```"}
