{"task_id": "Mbpp/141", "solution": "```python\ndef pancake_sort(input_list):\n    \"\"\"Sorts a list of integers using the pancake sort algorithm.\n    Returns a new list with elements in ascending order.\"\"\"\n    arr = list(input_list)\n    n = len(arr)\n\n    def _flip(arr_to_flip, k):\n        \"\"\"Reverses elements from index 0 up to k-1 in the list.\"\"\"\n        start = 0\n        end = k - 1\n        while start < end:\n            arr_to_flip[start], arr_to_flip[end] = arr_to_flip[end], arr_to_flip[start]\n            start += 1\n            end -= 1\n\n    for curr_size in range(n, 1, -1):\n        # Find index of the maximum element in the current unsorted part\n        max_idx = 0\n        for i in range(1, curr_size):\n            if arr[i] > arr[max_idx]:\n                max_idx = i\n\n        # If the maximum element is not in its correct sorted position\n        if max_idx != curr_size - 1:\n            # Move the maximum element to the front of the list\n            _flip(arr, max_idx + 1)\n            # Move the maximum element from the front to its correct sorted position\n            _flip(arr, curr_size)\n\n    return arr\n```\n"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/141", "solution": "def _flip(arr: list[int | float], i: int) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Reverses the order of elements in the sub-array arr[0...i] in-place.\n    This operation simulates flipping a stack of pancakes up to a certain point.\n    \"\"\"\n    start = 0\n    while start < i:\n        arr[start], arr[i] = arr[i], arr[start]\n        start += 1\n        i -= 1\n\ndef _find_max_index(arr: list[int | float], n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Finds the index of the largest element in arr[0...n-1].\n    It iterates through the specified prefix to locate the maximum value.\n    \"\"\"\n    max_val = arr[0]\n    max_idx = 0\n    for i in range(1, n):\n        if arr[i] > max_val:\n            max_val = arr[i]\n            max_idx = i\n    return max_idx\n\ndef pancake_sort(arr: list[int | float]) -> list[int | float]:\n    \"\"\"Sorts a list of numbers in ascending order using the pancake sort algorithm.\n    This function returns a new list containing the sorted elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    working_list = arr.copy()\n    n = len(working_list)\n\n    for current_size in range(n, 1, -1):\n        # Find the index of the maximum element in the current sub-array\n        max_index = _find_max_index(working_list, current_size)\n\n        # If the maximum element is not already at its correct sorted position\n        if max_index != current_size - 1:\n            # Move the maximum element to the beginning of the sub-array\n            _flip(working_list, max_index)\n            # Move the maximum element from the beginning to its correct sorted position\n            _flip(working_list, current_size - 1)\n\n    return working_list"}
