{"task_id": "Mbpp/160", "solution": "```python\ndef _extended_gcd(a: int, b: int) -> tuple[int, int, int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes gcd(a, b) and coefficients x, y such that ax + by = gcd(a, b).\n    This function uses the Extended Euclidean Algorithm recursively.\n    \"\"\"\n    if b == 0:\n        return (a, 1, 0)\n\n    gcd, x1, y1 = _extended_gcd(b, a % b)\n    x = y1\n    y = x1 - (a // b) * y1\n    return (gcd, x, y)\n\ndef find_solution(a: int, b: int, n: int) -> tuple[int, int] | None:\n    \"\"\"\n    Solves the linear Diophantine equation ax + by = n for integer solutions (x, y).\n    Returns a tuple (x, y) if a solution exists, otherwise returns None.\n    \"\"\"\n    gcd_val, x0, y0 = _extended_gcd(a, b)\n\n    # Handle the special case where a=0 and b=0. gcd(0,0) is 0.\n    if gcd_val == 0:\n        if n == 0:\n            return (0, 0) # 0x + 0y = 0 has infinite solutions, (0,0) is one.\n        else:\n            return None # 0x + 0y = n (n!=0) has no solution.\n\n    # For non-zero gcd_val, check if n is divisible by gcd_val.\n    if n % gcd_val != 0:\n        return None\n\n    # Calculate the particular solution.\n    k = n // gcd_val\n    x = x0 * k\n    y = y0 * k\n\n    return (x, y)\n```"}
