{"task_id": "Mbpp/166", "solution": "```python\ndef find_even_pair(input_list: list[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the number of pairs of integers in the input list\n    whose bitwise XOR operation results in an even number.\n    This is achieved by counting even and odd numbers separately and applying a combinatorial formula.\n    \"\"\"\n    even_count = 0\n    odd_count = 0\n\n    for num in input_list:\n        if num % 2 == 0:\n            even_count += 1\n        else:\n            odd_count += 1\n\n    # An XOR operation (A ^ B) results in an even number if A and B have the same parity.\n    # So, we count pairs of (even, even) and pairs of (odd, odd).\n    even_pairs = even_count * (even_count - 1) // 2\n    odd_pairs = odd_count * (odd_count - 1) // 2\n\n    return even_pairs + odd_pairs\n\n```"}
