{"task_id": "Mbpp/166", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List\n\ndef _is_even(number: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if a given integer is even.\n    Returns True if the number is even, False otherwise.\n    \"\"\"\n    return number % 2 == 0\n\ndef find_even_pair(numbers: List[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Counts pairs of integers in a list that XOR to an even number.\n    This uses the property that XOR of two numbers is even if they have the same parity.\n    \"\"\"\n    count_even = 0\n    count_odd = 0\n\n    for number in numbers:\n        if _is_even(number):\n            count_even += 1\n        else:\n            count_odd += 1\n\n    # Calculate combinations C(n, 2) for even numbers\n    pairs_even = count_even * (count_even - 1) // 2\n    # Calculate combinations C(n, 2) for odd numbers\n    pairs_odd = count_odd * (count_odd - 1) // 2\n\n    total_pairs = pairs_even + pairs_odd\n    return total_pairs\n```"}
