{"task_id": "Mbpp/223", "solution": "```python\ndef _find_first_occurrence(arr: list[int], n: int, element: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Finds the first occurrence of an element in a sorted array using binary search.\"\"\"\n    low, high = 0, n - 1\n    first_index = -1\n    while low <= high:\n        mid = low + (high - low) // 2\n        if arr[mid] == element:\n            first_index = mid\n            high = mid - 1  # Continue searching in the left half for an earlier occurrence\n        elif arr[mid] < element:\n            low = mid + 1\n        else:\n            high = mid - 1\n    return first_index\n\ndef _find_last_occurrence(arr: list[int], n: int, element: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Finds the last occurrence of an element in a sorted array using binary search.\"\"\"\n    low, high = 0, n - 1\n    last_index = -1\n    while low <= high:\n        mid = low + (high - low) // 2\n        if arr[mid] == element:\n            last_index = mid\n            low = mid + 1  # Continue searching in the right half for a later occurrence\n        elif arr[mid] < element:\n            low = mid + 1\n        else:\n            high = mid - 1\n    return last_index\n\ndef is_majority(arr: list[int], n: int, element: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Determines if an element is a majority element in a sorted array.\n    A majority element occurs strictly more than n/2 times.\n    \"\"\"\n    first_index = _find_first_occurrence(arr, n, element)\n    if first_index == -1:\n        return False\n\n    last_index = _find_last_occurrence(arr, n, element)\n    count = last_index - first_index + 1\n\n    return count > n / 2\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/222", "solution": "```python\ndef check_type(input_tuple: tuple) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if all elements in the input tuple have the same data type.\n    Returns True if all elements in the tuple have the same data type, False otherwise.\"\"\"\n    if not input_tuple or len(input_tuple) == 1:\n        return True\n\n    first_element_type = type(input_tuple[0])\n\n    for element in input_tuple[1:]:\n        if type(element) is not first_element_type:\n            return False\n\n    return True\n```"}
