{"task_id": "Mbpp/223", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List, Any\n\ndef _find_first_occurrence(arr: List[Any], n: int, element: Any) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Binary search to find the first index of 'element'.\n    Returns -1 if not found.\n    \"\"\"\n    low, high = 0, n - 1\n    result = -1\n    while low <= high:\n        mid = (low + high) // 2\n        if arr[mid] == element:\n            result = mid\n            high = mid - 1\n        elif arr[mid] < element:\n            low = mid + 1\n        else:\n            high = mid - 1\n    return result\n\ndef _find_last_occurrence(arr: List[Any], n: int, element: Any) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Binary search to find the last index of 'element'.\n    Returns -1 if not found.\n    \"\"\"\n    low, high = 0, n - 1\n    result = -1\n    while low <= high:\n        mid = (low + high) // 2\n        if arr[mid] == element:\n            result = mid\n            low = mid + 1\n        elif arr[mid] < element:\n            low = mid + 1\n        else:\n            high = mid - 1\n    return result\n\ndef is_majority(arr: List[Any], n: int, element: Any) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if 'element' is a majority element in 'arr' of length 'n'.\n    A majority element occurs strictly more than n/2 times.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return False\n\n    first_idx = _find_first_occurrence(arr, n, element)\n    if first_idx == -1:\n        return False\n\n    last_idx = _find_last_occurrence(arr, n, element)\n\n    count = last_idx - first_idx + 1\n\n    return count > n // 2\n```"}
