{"task_id": "Mbpp/232", "solution": "```python\nimport heapq\n\ndef larg_nnum(input_list: list, n: int) -> list:\n    \"\"\"Retrieves the 'n' largest items from a list, handling edge cases efficiently.\n    It uses heapq.nlargest for optimal performance in the general case.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    # Handle edge cases where n is non-positive or the input list is empty.\n    if n <= 0 or not input_list:\n        return []\n\n    list_len = len(input_list)\n\n    # If n is greater than the number of elements, return all elements.\n    # The design specifies sorting in descending order for consistency.\n    if n > list_len:\n        return sorted(input_list, reverse=True)\n\n    # For the general case, use heapq.nlargest for efficient retrieval.\n    # This finds the 'n' largest elements without fully sorting the list.\n    return heapq.nlargest(n, input_list)\n```"}
