{"task_id": "Mbpp/247", "solution": "```python\ndef lps(input_string: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the length of the longest palindromic subsequence in the given string.\n\n    Args:\n        input_string: The string for which to calculate the LPS length.\n\n    Returns:\n        An integer representing the length of the longest palindromic subsequence.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(input_string)\n    # Create a DP table to store results of subproblems\n    # dp[i][j] stores the length of LPS for substring input_string[i...j]\n    dp = [[0] * n for _ in range(n)]\n\n    # Palindromic subsequence of length 1 is 1\n    for i in range(n):\n        dp[i][i] = 1\n\n    # Fill the table. l is length of substring\n    for l in range(2, n + 1):\n        for i in range(n - l + 1):\n            j = i + l - 1\n            if input_string[i] == input_string[j] and l == 2:\n                dp[i][j] = 2\n            elif input_string[i] == input_string[j]:\n                dp[i][j] = 2 + dp[i + 1][j - 1]\n            else:\n                dp[i][j] = max(dp[i][j - 1], dp[i + 1][j])\n\n    return dp[0][n - 1]\n```"}
