{"task_id": "Mbpp/245", "solution": "```python\ndef max_sum(arr: list) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the maximum sum of a bitonic subsequence for the given array.\n    A bitonic sequence is first increasing then decreasing (purely increasing/decreasing are also bitonic).\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(arr)\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n\n    # Calculate Longest Increasing Subsequence (LIS) sum ending at each index\n    lis_sum = list(arr)\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(i):\n            if arr[i] > arr[j]:\n                lis_sum[i] = max(lis_sum[i], lis_sum[j] + arr[i])\n\n    # Calculate Longest Decreasing Subsequence (LDS) sum starting at each index\n    lds_sum = list(arr)\n    for i in range(n - 1, -1, -1):\n        for j in range(n - 1, i, -1):\n            if arr[i] > arr[j]:\n                lds_sum[i] = max(lds_sum[i], lds_sum[j] + arr[i])\n\n    # Calculate maximum bitonic sum\n    # arr[i] is subtracted once because it's counted in both lis_sum[i] and lds_sum[i].\n    max_bitonic_sum = 0\n    for i in range(n):\n        current_bitonic_sum = lis_sum[i] + lds_sum[i] - arr[i]\n        max_bitonic_sum = max(max_bitonic_sum, current_bitonic_sum)\n\n    return max(0, max_bitonic_sum)\n```"}
