{"task_id": "Mbpp/245", "solution": "```python\ndef _calculate_lis_sums(arr: list[int | float]) -> list[int | float]:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the maximum sum of an increasing subsequence ending at each position.\"\"\"\n    n = len(arr)\n    if n == 0:\n        return []\n    lis_sums = list(arr)\n\n    for i in range(1, n):\n        for j in range(i):\n            if arr[i] > arr[j]:\n                lis_sums[i] = max(lis_sums[i], lis_sums[j] + arr[i])\n    return lis_sums\n\ndef _calculate_lds_sums(arr: list[int | float]) -> list[int | float]:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the maximum sum of a decreasing subsequence starting at each position.\"\"\"\n    n = len(arr)\n    if n == 0:\n        return []\n    lds_sums = list(arr)\n\n    for i in range(n - 2, -1, -1):\n        for j in range(i + 1, n):\n            if arr[i] > arr[j]:\n                lds_sums[i] = max(lds_sums[i], arr[i] + lds_sums[j])\n    return lds_sums\n\ndef max_sum(arr: list[int | float]) -> int | float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the maximum sum of a bitonic subsequence within the input array.\n    A bitonic subsequence first increases and then decreases.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(arr)\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n    if n == 1:\n        return arr[0]\n\n    lis_sums = _calculate_lis_sums(arr)\n    lds_sums = _calculate_lds_sums(arr)\n\n    max_bitonic_sum = float('-inf')\n\n    # A bitonic subsequence can be formed by combining an LIS ending at arr[i]\n    # and an LDS starting at arr[i], with arr[i] as the peak.\n    for i in range(n):\n        current_bitonic_sum = lis_sums[i] + lds_sums[i] - arr[i]\n        max_bitonic_sum = max(max_bitonic_sum, current_bitonic_sum)\n\n    return max_bitonic_sum\n```"}
