{"task_id": "Mbpp/256", "solution": "```python\ndef _is_prime(number):\n    \"\"\"Checks if a number is prime using trial division up to its square root.\"\"\"\n    if number < 2:\n        return False\n    if number == 2:\n        return True\n    if number % 2 == 0:\n        return False\n    i = 3\n    while i * i <= number:\n        if number % i == 0:\n            return False\n        i += 2\n    return True\n\ndef count_Primes_nums(n):\n    \"\"\"Counts prime numbers strictly less than n. Raises ValueError for negative input.\"\"\"\n    if n < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input must be non-negative\")\n\n    if n < 2:\n        return 0\n\n    prime_count = 0\n    for num in range(2, n):\n        if _is_prime(num):\n            prime_count += 1\n    return prime_count\n```"}
