{"task_id": "Mbpp/247", "solution": "```python\ndef lps(s: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the length of the longest palindromic subsequence in the given string.\n    Uses dynamic programming to build up solutions for substrings.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(s)\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n\n    # dp[i][j] stores the length of the LPS for substring s[i...j]\n    dp = [[0] * n for _ in range(n)]\n\n    # All single characters are palindromic subsequences of length 1\n    for i in range(n):\n        dp[i][i] = 1\n\n    # Fill the DP table for lengths from 2 to n\n    for length in range(2, n + 1):\n        for i in range(n - length + 1):\n            j = i + length - 1\n            if s[i] == s[j]:\n                dp[i][j] = 2 + dp[i + 1][j - 1] if length > 2 else 2\n            else:\n                dp[i][j] = max(dp[i + 1][j], dp[i][j - 1])\n\n    return dp[0][n - 1]\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/259", "solution": "```python\ndef _validate_input_structure(tuple1, tuple2):\n    \"\"\"Validates the structural integrity of input tuples.\n    Raises ValueError if outer or inner tuple dimensions do not match.\"\"\"\n    if len(tuple1) != len(tuple2):\n        raise ValueError(\"Input tuples must have an equal number of inner tuples.\")\n\n    for i in range(len(tuple1)):\n        if len(tuple1[i]) != len(tuple2[i]):\n            raise ValueError(\"Corresponding inner tuples must have an equal number of elements.\")\n    return True\n\ndef maximize_elements(tuple1, tuple2):\n    \"\"\"Calculates the element-wise maximum of two nested tuples.\n    The function requires structurally identical input tuples of tuples.\"\"\"\n    _validate_input_structure(tuple1, tuple2)\n\n    maximized_outer_tuple_elements = []\n    for inner_tuple1, inner_tuple2 in zip(tuple1, tuple2):\n        current_maximized_inner_tuple_elements = []\n        for element1, element2 in zip(inner_tuple1, inner_tuple2):\n            current_maximized_inner_tuple_elements.append(max(element1, element2))\n        maximized_outer_tuple_elements.append(tuple(current_maximized_inner_tuple_elements))\n\n    return tuple(maximized_outer_tuple_elements)\n```"}
