{"task_id": "Mbpp/260", "solution": "def _is_prime(num: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Determines if a given number is prime.\"\"\"\n    if num < 2:\n        return False\n    if num == 2:\n        return True\n    if num % 2 == 0:\n        return False\n    i = 3\n    while i * i <= num:\n        if num % i == 0:\n            return False\n        i += 2\n    return True\n\ndef _calculate_nsw_number(k: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the k-th Newman-Shanks-Williams number.\"\"\"\n    if k == 0:\n        return 1\n    if k == 1:\n        return 1\n    s_prev2 = 1 # S_0\n    s_prev1 = 1 # S_1\n    for _ in range(2, k + 1):\n        current_s = 2 * s_prev1 + s_prev2\n        s_prev2 = s_prev1\n        s_prev1 = current_s\n    return s_prev1\n\ndef newman_prime(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates and returns the nth Newman-Shanks-Williams prime number.\n    Based on the assertion newman_prime(3) == 7, 'n' is interpreted as the index 'k' for S_k.\n    It is assumed that for the given 'n', the corresponding Newman-Shanks-Williams number S_n will be prime.\n    \"\"\"\n    nsw_number = _calculate_nsw_number(n)\n    return nsw_number"}
