{"task_id": "Mbpp/256", "solution": "```python\ndef _is_prime(num: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if a number is prime using an optimized trial division method.\n    It handles small primes and checks divisibility up to its square root.\n    \"\"\"\n    if num < 2:\n        return False\n    if num == 2 or num == 3:\n        return True\n    if num % 2 == 0 or num % 3 == 0:\n        return False\n    i = 5\n    while i * i <= num:\n        if num % i == 0 or num % (i + 2) == 0:\n            return False\n        i += 6\n    return True\n\ndef count_Primes_nums(limit: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts the number of prime numbers strictly less than the given limit.\n    It iterates through numbers from 2 up to limit-1, checking each for primality.\n    \"\"\"\n    prime_count = 0\n    for num in range(2, limit):\n        if _is_prime(num):\n            prime_count += 1\n    return prime_count\n```"}
