{"task_id": "Mbpp/283", "solution": "```python\nimport collections\n\ndef validate(number):\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if the frequency of each digit in an integer is less than or equal to the digit itself.\n    Uses collections.Counter for efficient digit frequency calculation.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Convert the absolute value of the number to a string to easily iterate over digits.\n    s_number = str(abs(number))\n\n    # Calculate the frequency of each digit.\n    digit_frequencies = collections.Counter(s_number)\n\n    # Iterate through each digit and its frequency.\n    for char_digit, frequency in digit_frequencies.items():\n        # Convert the character digit back to an integer for comparison.\n        digit_value = int(char_digit)\n\n        # Check if the frequency of the digit exceeds its numerical value.\n        if frequency > digit_value:\n            return False  # If any digit fails the condition, return False immediately.\n\n    # If all digits pass the validation, return True.\n    return True\n```"}
