{"task_id": "Mbpp/296", "solution": "```python\ndef get_Inv_Count(arr):\n    \"\"\"Counts inversions in the input array using a modified merge sort algorithm.\n    An inversion is a pair (i, j) such that i < j and A[i] > A[j].\"\"\"\n\n    def _merge_and_count(arr_slice):\n        n = len(arr_slice)\n        if n <= 1:\n            return arr_slice, 0\n\n        mid = n // 2\n        left_half, left_inversions = _merge_and_count(arr_slice[:mid])\n        right_half, right_inversions = _merge_and_count(arr_slice[mid:])\n\n        merged_arr = []\n        inversions = left_inversions + right_inversions\n        i, j = 0, 0\n        len_left = len(left_half)\n        len_right = len(right_half)\n\n        while i < len_left and j < len_right:\n            if left_half[i] <= right_half[j]:\n                merged_arr.append(left_half[i])\n                i += 1\n            else:\n                merged_arr.append(right_half[j])\n                j += 1\n                inversions += (len_left - i)\n\n        merged_arr.extend(left_half[i:])\n        merged_arr.extend(right_half[j:])\n\n        return merged_arr, inversions\n\n    _, total_inversions = _merge_and_count(list(arr))\n    return total_inversions\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/296", "solution": "```python\ndef get_Inv_Count(arr: list[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the total number of inversions in the given array.\n\n    An inversion is a pair of indices (i, j) such that i < j and arr[i] > arr[j].\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(arr)\n    inversion_count = 0\n    for i in range(n - 1):\n        for j in range(i + 1, n):\n            if arr[i] > arr[j]:\n                inversion_count += 1\n    return inversion_count\n```"}
