{"task_id": "Mbpp/300", "solution": "```python\nimport itertools\n\ndef count_binary_seq(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the count of binary sequences of length 2n where the sum of the first n bits\n    equals the sum of the last n bits. It iterates through all possible sequences.\n    \"\"\"\n    total_count = 0\n    sequence_length = 2 * n\n\n    # Generate all binary sequences of length 2n.\n    for sequence in itertools.product([0, 1], repeat=sequence_length):\n        first_n_bits_sum = sum(sequence[:n])\n        last_n_bits_sum = sum(sequence[n:])\n\n        if first_n_bits_sum == last_n_bits_sum:\n            total_count += 1\n\n    return total_count\n```\n"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/299", "solution": "```python\ndef max_aggregate(data: list[tuple[str, int]]) -> tuple[str, int]:\n    \"\"\"Aggregates scores by name and finds the name with the maximum total score.\n    Returns the name and its total score, or ('', 0) if the input list is empty.\n    \"\"\"\n    aggregated_scores = {}\n    for name, score in data:\n        aggregated_scores[name] = aggregated_scores.get(name, 0) + score\n\n    if not aggregated_scores:\n        return ('', 0)\n\n    max_name, max_score = max(aggregated_scores.items(), key=lambda item: item[1])\n\n    return (max_name, max_score)\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/300", "solution": "```python\ndef count_binary_seq(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the count of binary sequences of length 2n where first n bits sum equals last n bits sum.\n    This count is equivalent to the central binomial coefficient (2n choose n).\n    \"\"\"\n    def _combinations(n_val: int, k_val: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Computes the binomial coefficient C(n_val, k_val) = n_val! / (k_val! * (n_val - k_val)!).\n        Handles edge cases for k_val outside the valid range or being 0/n_val.\n        \"\"\"\n        if k_val < 0 or k_val > n_val:\n            return 0\n        if k_val == 0 or k_val == n_val:\n            return 1\n        if k_val > n_val // 2:\n            k_val = n_val - k_val\n\n        result = 1\n        for i in range(k_val):\n            result = result * (n_val - i) // (i + 1)\n        return result\n\n    # The problem's solution is the central binomial coefficient C(2n, n).\n    return _combinations(2 * n, n)\n```\n"}
