{"task_id": "Mbpp/305", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List, Tuple\n\ndef start_withp(input_strings: List[str]) -> Tuple[str, str]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Extracts the first two words starting with 'p' or 'P' from a list of strings.\n    Raises ValueError if fewer than two such words are found.\n    \"\"\"\n    p_words_found = []\n\n    for s in input_strings:\n        words = s.split()\n        for word in words:\n            if word.lower().startswith('p'):\n                p_words_found.append(word)\n                if len(p_words_found) == 2:\n                    break # Stop collecting after two words\n        if len(p_words_found) == 2:\n            break # Stop processing strings after two words are found\n\n    if len(p_words_found) < 2:\n        raise ValueError(\"Fewer than two words starting with 'p' or 'P' were found.\")\n    else:\n        return (p_words_found[0], p_words_found[1])\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/306", "solution": "```python\ndef max_sum_increasing_subseq(array: list[int], size: int, i: int, k: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the maximum sum of an increasing subsequence from a prefix up to index i,\n    always including the element at index k (where k > i). Returns -1 for invalid inputs.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Input validation: check if i and k are within array bounds.\n    if not (0 <= i < size and 0 <= k < size):\n        return -1\n\n    # Input validation: ensure k is strictly greater than i.\n    if not (k > i):\n        return -1\n\n    # Compute maximum sum of an increasing subsequence ending at each index up to i.\n    # dp[idx] stores the maximum sum of an increasing subsequence ending at array[idx].\n    dp = [0] * (i + 1)\n    for current_idx in range(i + 1):\n        dp[current_idx] = array[current_idx]\n        for prev_idx in range(current_idx):\n            if array[current_idx] > array[prev_idx]:\n                dp[current_idx] = max(dp[current_idx], dp[prev_idx] + array[current_idx])\n\n    # Initialize max_sum_so_far with array[k], as it must be included.\n    max_sum_so_far = array[k]\n\n    # Iterate through prefix sums to combine with array[k].\n    for current_idx in range(i + 1):\n        if array[current_idx] < array[k]:\n            max_sum_so_far = max(max_sum_so_far, dp[current_idx] + array[k])\n\n    return max_sum_so_far\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/308", "solution": "```python\ndef large_product(list1, list2, k):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the k largest products by pairing numbers from two input lists.\n    Returns these k products in descending order.\n    \"\"\"\n    all_products = []\n    for n1 in list1:\n        for n2 in list2:\n            all_products.append(n1 * n2)\n\n    all_products.sort(reverse=True)\n    return all_products[:k]\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/308", "solution": "```python\ndef large_product(list1: list[int], list2: list[int], n: int) -> list[int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the 'n' largest products formed by taking one element from each input list.\n    Handles empty lists or n=0 by returning an empty list.\n    \"\"\"\n    all_products = []\n\n    # Handle edge cases: empty lists or n being zero.\n    if not list1 or not list2 or n == 0:\n        return []\n\n    # Generate all possible products.\n    for num1 in list1:\n        for num2 in list2:\n            all_products.append(num1 * num2)\n\n    # Sort the products in descending order.\n    all_products.sort(reverse=True)\n\n    # Return the first 'n' largest products.\n    return all_products[:n]\n```"}
