{"task_id": "Mbpp/311", "solution": "```python\ndef _find_leftmost_unset_bit_position(num: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Identifies the position of the leftmost unset bit in the given non-negative integer.\n    Iterates from the most significant bit downwards to find the first zero bit.\n    \"\"\"\n    if num == 0:\n        return 0\n\n    # Find the position of the most significant set bit.\n    # num.bit_length() gives the number of bits required to represent the integer in binary,\n    # so msb_pos is (bit_length - 1).\n    msb_pos = num.bit_length() - 1\n\n    # Iterate from the MSB position down to 0\n    for k in range(msb_pos, -1, -1):\n        if (num >> k) & 1 == 0:\n            return k\n\n    # If all bits up to msb_pos are set (e.g., num = 7, binary 111),\n    # the leftmost unset bit is at msb_pos + 1.\n    return msb_pos + 1\n\n\ndef set_left_most_unset_bit(num: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Sets the leftmost unset bit in the given integer.\n    For negative numbers, the original number is returned.\n    \"\"\"\n    if num < 0:\n        return num\n\n    bit_pos_to_set = _find_leftmost_unset_bit_position(num)\n    return num | (1 << bit_pos_to_set)\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/299", "solution": "```python\nfrom collections import defaultdict\n\ndef max_aggregate(scores_list: list[tuple[str, int]]) -> tuple[str, int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the maximum aggregate score from a list of name-score tuples.\n    Returns the name with the highest total score and their score, or (\"\", 0) if the list is empty.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not scores_list:\n        return \"\", 0\n\n    aggregate_scores = defaultdict(int)\n    for name, score in scores_list:\n        aggregate_scores[name] += score\n\n    if not aggregate_scores:\n        return \"\", 0\n\n    max_name = \"\"\n    max_score = -1\n\n    for name, total_score in aggregate_scores.items():\n        if total_score > max_score:\n            max_score = total_score\n            max_name = name\n\n    return max_name, max_score\n```"}
