{"task_id": "Mbpp/389", "solution": "```python\ndef find_lucas(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the n'th Lucas number.\n    The sequence is defined by L(0)=2, L(1)=1, and L(n)=L(n-1)+L(n-2) for n > 1.\n    \"\"\"\n    # The input 'n' for Lucas number calculation must be a non-negative integer.\n    # As per SRS, n will always be non-negative, so no error handling for negative n is required.\n\n    if n == 0:\n        return 2\n    elif n == 1:\n        return 1\n    else:\n        a, b = 2, 1  # Initialize with L(0) and L(1) for iterative calculation.\n        for _ in range(2, n + 1):\n            a, b = b, a + b\n        return b\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/306", "solution": "```python\ndef max_sum_increasing_subseq(nums: list[int], n: int, i: int, k: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the maximum sum of an increasing subsequence from nums[0...i]\n    that includes nums[k] and maximizes the total sum.\n    \"\"\"\n    dp = [0] * (i + 1)\n    overall_max_prefix_sum = 0\n\n    for j in range(i + 1):\n        if nums[j] < nums[k]:\n            current_max_sum_for_j = nums[j]\n            for p in range(j):\n                if nums[j] > nums[p]:\n                    current_max_sum_for_j = max(current_max_sum_for_j, dp[p] + nums[j])\n            dp[j] = current_max_sum_for_j\n            overall_max_prefix_sum = max(overall_max_prefix_sum, dp[j])\n        else:\n            dp[j] = 0\n\n    return overall_max_prefix_sum + nums[k]\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/311", "solution": "```python\ndef set_left_most_unset_bit(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Sets the leftmost unset bit of an integer n.\n\n    If all relevant bits of n are set, n is returned unchanged.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == -1:\n        return n\n\n    if n == 0:\n        return 1  # The leftmost unset bit for 0 is at position 0.\n\n    # Find the position of the most significant bit (MSB).\n    # n.bit_length() gives the number of bits required to represent n, so MSB is at index bit_length - 1.\n    msb_pos = n.bit_length() - 1\n\n    # Iterate from the MSB position downwards to find the leftmost unset bit.\n    for k in range(msb_pos, -1, -1):\n        # Check if the k-th bit is 0 (unset).\n        if (n & (1 << k)) == 0:\n            # If unset, set this bit and return the new number.\n            return n | (1 << k)\n\n    # If the loop completes, it means all bits from MSB down to 0 are set.\n    # In this case, the leftmost unset bit is at the position immediately to the left of the MSB.\n    return n | (1 << (msb_pos + 1))\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/389", "solution": "```python\ndef find_lucas(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the n'th Lucas number iteratively.\n    L(0) = 2, L(1) = 1, and L(k) = L(k-1) + L(k-2) for k > 1.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 2\n    if n == 1:\n        return 1\n\n    a, b = 2, 1  # Initialize with L(0) and L(1)\n    for _ in range(2, n + 1):\n        next_lucas = a + b\n        a = b\n        b = next_lucas\n    return b\n```"}
