{"task_id": "Mbpp/392", "solution": "```python\ndef get_max_sum(n: int) -> int:\n    memo = {}\n\n    def _f(k: int) -> int:\n        # Base case: If k is 0 or negative, its contribution to the sum is 0.\n        if k <= 0:\n            return 0\n        # Memoization check: Return the stored result if k has been computed before.\n        if k in memo:\n            return memo[k]\n\n        # Recursive step: Calculate the sum from its parts.\n        sum_of_recursive_parts = _f(k // 2) + _f(k // 3) + _f(k // 4) + _f(k // 5)\n\n        # The result for f(k) is the maximum of k itself or the sum of its parts.\n        result = max(k, sum_of_recursive_parts)\n\n        # Store the computed result in memo and then return it.\n        memo[k] = result\n        return result\n\n    return _f(n)\n```"}
