{"task_id": "Mbpp/392", "solution": "```python\ndef get_max_sum(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the maximum sum for n using a recursive formula with memoization.\"\"\"\n    memo = {} # Initialize memoization dictionary for this call.\n\n    def _calculate_max_sum(current_n: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Helper function to recursively calculate max sum and store results.\"\"\"\n        if current_n in memo:\n            return memo[current_n]\n\n        if current_n == 0:\n            memo[0] = 0\n            return 0\n\n        # Recursively calculate sum of parts using integer division.\n        sum_of_parts = (_calculate_max_sum(current_n // 2) +\n                        _calculate_max_sum(current_n // 3) +\n                        _calculate_max_sum(current_n // 4) +\n                        _calculate_max_sum(current_n // 5))\n\n        # Determine the maximum between the sum of parts and current_n itself.\n        result = max(sum_of_parts, current_n)\n\n        memo[current_n] = result\n        return result\n\n    return _calculate_max_sum(n)\n```\n"}
