{"task_id": "Mbpp/440", "solution": "```python\nimport re\n\ndef _strip_trailing_punctuation(word: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Strips trailing punctuation characters from a word.\"\"\"\n    PUNCTUATION_CHARS = \".,;:!?\\'\\\"-()[]{}/\\\\\\\\`~@#$%^&*_+=|<>\"\n    while word and word[-1] in PUNCTUATION_CHARS:\n        word = word[:-1]\n    return word\n\ndef _is_adverb(word: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Determines if a given word is an adverb using heuristics.\"\"\"\n    word_lower = word.lower()\n\n    # Common adverbs including irregular forms or those not ending in -ly.\n    common_adverbs = {\n        \"very\", \"never\", \"always\", \"here\", \"there\", \"now\", \"then\", \"often\", \"seldom\",\n        \"well\", \"fast\", \"hard\", \"late\", \"soon\", \"already\", \"still\", \"just\", \"quite\",\n        \"rather\", \"too\", \"enough\", \"almost\", \"only\", \"even\", \"back\", \"away\", \"out\",\n        \"up\", \"down\", \"around\", \"inside\", \"outside\", \"everywhere\", \"somewhere\",\n        \"anywhere\", \"nowhere\", \"today\", \"yesterday\", \"tomorrow\"\n    }\n\n    if word_lower in common_adverbs:\n        return True\n\n    # Heuristic: check for words ending in \\\"-ly\\\", as many adverbs do.\n    if word_lower.endswith(\"ly\") and len(word_lower) > 2:\n        return True\n\n    return False\n\ndef find_adverb_position(sentence: str) -> tuple:\n    \"\"\"\n    Identifies the first adverb and its position within a sentence.\n    Returns (startIndex, endIndex, adverb) or (-1, -1, '') if no adverb is found.\n    \"\"\"\n    found_start_index = -1\n    found_end_index = -1\n    found_adverb_text = ''\n\n    current_pos = 0\n    sentence_length = len(sentence)\n\n    while current_pos < sentence_length:\n        # Skip any leading whitespace before the next potential word\n        while current_pos < sentence_length and sentence[current_pos].isspace():\n            current_pos += 1\n\n        if current_pos >= sentence_length:\n            break # Reached the end of the sentence\n\n        word_start_index = current_pos\n        # Find the end of the current word (sequence of non-space characters)\n        word_end_index = word_start_index\n        while word_end_index < sentence_length and not sentence[word_end_index].isspace():\n            word_end_index += 1\n\n        # Extract the raw token, including any attached punctuation\n        raw_token = sentence[word_start_index:word_end_index]\n\n        # Clean the token by stripping trailing punctuation\n        cleaned_token = _strip_trailing_punctuation(raw_token)\n\n        # Check if the cleaned token is an adverb\n        if _is_adverb(cleaned_token):\n            found_start_index = word_start_index\n            # The endIndex is exclusive and refers to the end of the cleaned adverb in the original string.\n            found_end_index = word_start_index + len(cleaned_token)\n            found_adverb_text = cleaned_token\n            break # The first adverb has been found, terminate search\n\n        current_pos = word_end_index # Move to the position after the current word\n\n    return (found_start_index, found_end_index, found_adverb_text)\n```\n"}
