{"task_id": "Mbpp/440", "solution": "```python\nimport re\nimport string\n\ndef find_adverb_position(sentence: str):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the first adverb in a given sentence and returns its start position,\n    end position, and the adverb itself. Adverbs are identified by ending in 'ly'.\n    Punctuation attached to the word is removed for adverb identification,\n    and the returned adverb string is clean (without punctuation).\n\n    Args:\n        sentence: The input string sentence to search for an adverb.\n\n    Returns:\n        A tuple (start_index, end_index, adverb_text) if an adverb is found.\n        Returns None if no adverb is found in the sentence.\n        The indices are 0-based and correspond to the position of the clean\n        adverb within the original sentence.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Define a set of punctuation characters to strip\n    # string.punctuation includes !\"#$%&'()*+,-./:;<=>?@[\\]^_`{|}~\n    punctuation_chars = string.punctuation\n    adverb_suffix = \"ly\"\n\n    i = 0\n    while i < len(sentence):\n        # Skip leading non-alphanumeric characters (including spaces and punctuation)\n        while i < len(sentence) and not sentence[i].isalnum():\n            i += 1\n\n        if i == len(sentence):\n            break  # Reached end of sentence\n\n        word_start_index = i\n        # Find the end of the current word-like token. This token can include\n        # alphanumeric characters and potentially trailing punctuation,\n        # stopping at the next space or end of sentence.\n        while i < len(sentence) and sentence[i] != ' ':\n            i += 1\n        word_end_index = i\n\n        # Extract the raw token (e.g., \"clearly!!\" or \"quickly.\")\n        raw_token = sentence[word_start_index:word_end_index]\n\n        # Clean the token by stripping trailing punctuation for adverb check\n        # For example, \"clearly!!\" becomes \"clearly\"\n        clean_word = raw_token.rstrip(punctuation_chars)\n\n        # Check if the clean word is a potential adverb (ends with 'ly')\n        if clean_word and clean_word.lower().endswith(adverb_suffix):\n            # Found the first adverb\n            adverb_text = clean_word\n\n            # The start index is the beginning of the raw token in the sentence.\n            # The end index is the start index plus the length of the *clean* adverb text.\n            adverb_end_index = word_start_index + len(adverb_text)\n\n            return (word_start_index, adverb_end_index, adverb_text)\n\n    return None\n```"}
