{"task_id": "Mbpp/447", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List\n\nclass Number:\n    \"\"\"\n    Represents a single numeric value.\n    Provides a method to calculate its cube.\n    \"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, value: int):\n        self._value = value\n\n    def calculate_cube(self) -> int:\n        \"\"\"\n        Computes and returns the cube of the stored value.\n        \"\"\"\n        return self._value ** 3\n\nclass NumberList:\n    \"\"\"\n    Manages a collection of Number objects.\n    Provides functionality to get a list of their cubed values.\n    \"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, numbers: List[int]):\n        self._elements: List[Number] = [Number(num) for num in numbers]\n\n    def get_cube_list(self) -> List[int]:\n        \"\"\"\n        Iterates through its Number objects and returns a new list of their cubed values.\n        The order of elements is maintained.\n        \"\"\"\n        return [element.calculate_cube() for element in self._elements]\n\ndef cube_nums(input_list: List[int]) -> List[int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the cube of each individual element in a list of numbers.\n    Returns a new list containing the cube of each element from the input_list,\n    maintaining the original order.\n    \"\"\"\n    number_list_processor = NumberList(input_list)\n    return number_list_processor.get_cube_list()\n```"}
