{"task_id": "Mbpp/556", "solution": "```python\ndef find_Odd_Pair(input_list: list[int], length: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts pairs in a list whose XOR value is odd.\n    An XOR operation is odd if and only if one operand is even and the other is odd.\n    \"\"\"\n    even_count = 0\n    odd_count = 0\n\n    # Iterate through the input list to count even and odd numbers.\n    for number in input_list:\n        if number % 2 == 0:\n            even_count += 1\n        else:\n            odd_count += 1\n\n    # The total number of odd XOR pairs is the product of the count of even and odd numbers.\n    total_pairs = even_count * odd_count\n    return total_pairs\n```"}
