{"task_id": "Mbpp/559", "solution": "```python\ndef max_sub_array_sum(arr: list[int], n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the sum of the largest contiguous sublist using Kadane's Algorithm.\n    It iterates through the array, tracking the current maximum sum and the overall maximum.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n\n    global_max_so_far = arr[0]\n    current_max_ending_here = arr[0]\n\n    for i in range(1, n):\n        current_max_ending_here = max(arr[i], current_max_ending_here + arr[i])\n        global_max_so_far = max(global_max_so_far, current_max_ending_here)\n\n    return global_max_so_far\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/558", "solution": "```python\ndef _get_digits(number: int) -> list[int]:\n    \"\"\"Extracts digits from an integer, from least significant to most significant.\n    Handles negative numbers by taking absolute value for digit extraction.\n    \"\"\"\n    if number == 0:\n        return [0]\n    digits = []\n    abs_number = abs(number)\n    while abs_number > 0:\n        digits.append(abs_number % 10)\n        abs_number //= 10\n    return digits\n\ndef digit_distance_nums(num1: int, num2: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the sum of per-digit absolute differences between two integers.\n    Missing digits are treated as zero for comparison.\n    \"\"\"\n    digits1 = _get_digits(num1)\n    digits2 = _get_digits(num2)\n\n    max_len = max(len(digits1), len(digits2))\n    total_sum = 0\n\n    for i in range(max_len):\n        digit1 = digits1[i] if i < len(digits1) else 0\n        digit2 = digits2[i] if i < len(digits2) else 0\n        total_sum += abs(digit1 - digit2)\n\n    return total_sum\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/559", "solution": "```python\ndef max_sub_array_sum(input_list, input_integer):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of the largest contiguous sublist using Kadane's algorithm.\n    The `input_integer` parameter is provided as per specification but not used in the core logic.\n    \"\"\"\n    current_max_sum = 0\n    global_max_sum = float('-inf')\n\n    for element in input_list:\n        current_max_sum = max(element, current_max_sum + element)\n        global_max_sum = max(global_max_sum, current_max_sum)\n\n    return global_max_sum\n```"}
