{"task_id": "Mbpp/566", "solution": "def sum_digits(number: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of the digits of a non-negative integer.\n\n    Args:\n        number: A non-negative integer.\n\n    Returns:\n        The sum of the digits of the input number.\n\n    Raises:\n        TypeError: If the input is not an integer.\n        ValueError: If the input is a negative integer.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(number, int):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input must be an integer\")\n    if number < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input must be a non-negative integer\")\n\n    total_sum = 0\n    # Convert the integer to a string to easily iterate over its digits.\n    # This also handles the edge case of number being 0 correctly (sum is 0).\n    for digit_char in str(number):\n        total_sum += int(digit_char)\n    return total_sum"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/567", "solution": "def issort_list(input_list: list) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if a list is sorted in non-decreasing order.\n    Returns True for empty or single-element lists.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(input_list)\n\n    # Handle edge cases: empty list or list with a single element.\n    if n <= 1:\n        return True\n\n    # Iterate through the list, comparing adjacent elements.\n    for i in range(n - 1):\n        if input_list[i] > input_list[i+1]:\n            return False\n\n    # If no unsorted pair is found, the list is sorted.\n    return True"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/567", "solution": "```python\ndef issort_list(lst):\n    \"\"\"Checks if a list is sorted in non-decreasing order.\n    Returns True if sorted, False otherwise.\"\"\"\n    n = len(lst)\n\n    # An empty or single-element list is considered sorted.\n    if n <= 1:\n        return True\n\n    # Iterate through adjacent pairs to check for non-decreasing order.\n    for i in range(n - 1):\n        if lst[i] > lst[i+1]:\n            return False  # Found an element greater than its successor.\n\n    return True  # All adjacent elements are in non-decreasing order.\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/566", "solution": "```python\ndef sum_digits(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of the digits of a non-negative integer.\n\n    Args:\n        n: A non-negative integer.\n\n    Returns:\n        The sum of the digits of n.\n\n    Raises:\n        ValueError: If n is a negative integer.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input must be a non-negative integer.\")\n    return sum(int(digit) for digit in str(n))\n```"}
