{"task_id": "Mbpp/577", "solution": "```python\ndef last_Digit_Factorial(number: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the last digit of the factorial for a given positive integer.\n    For numbers 5 or greater, the last digit of their factorial is always 0.\n    \"\"\"\n    if number >= 5:\n        return 0\n\n    factorial_result = 1\n    for i in range(1, number + 1):\n        factorial_result *= i\n\n    return factorial_result % 10\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/579", "solution": "```python\ndef find_dissimilar(tuple1: tuple, tuple2: tuple) -> tuple:\n    \"\"\"\n    Identifies and returns elements unique to each of the two input tuples.\n    Elements are combined and sorted to ensure consistent output order.\n    \"\"\"\n    set1 = set(tuple1)\n    set2 = set(tuple2)\n\n    # Elements unique to tuple1\n    unique_to_tuple1 = set1 - set2\n\n    # Elements unique to tuple2\n    unique_to_tuple2 = set2 - set1\n\n    # Combine all unique elements and sort them for consistent output\n    combined_unique_elements = unique_to_tuple1.union(unique_to_tuple2)\n    return tuple(sorted(list(combined_unique_elements)))\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/578", "solution": "```python\ndef interleave_lists(list1: list, list2: list, list3: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"Interleaves three input lists of the same length into a single flat list.\n    Elements are taken sequentially from the first, second, then third list.\n    \"\"\"\n    interleaved_list = []\n    length = len(list1)  # Assume all lists are of the same length\n\n    for i in range(length):\n        interleaved_list.append(list1[i])\n        interleaved_list.append(list2[i])\n        interleaved_list.append(list3[i])\n\n    return interleaved_list\n```"}
