{"task_id": "Mbpp/589", "solution": "```python\nimport math\n\ndef perfect_squares(num1: int, num2: int) -> list[int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Identifies and returns a list of all perfect squares within the specified inclusive range [num1, num2].\n    The list is empty if no perfect squares are found or if num1 > num2.\n    \"\"\"\n    result_list = []\n\n    if num1 > num2:\n        return result_list\n\n    # Calculate the starting and ending square roots for the iteration range.\n    # max(0, x) ensures sqrt is not called with negative numbers, as perfect squares are non-negative.\n    start_sqrt = int(math.ceil(math.sqrt(max(0, num1))))\n    end_sqrt = int(math.floor(math.sqrt(max(0, num2))))\n\n    # Iterate through possible integer square roots and add their squares if they fall within the range.\n    for i in range(start_sqrt, end_sqrt + 1):\n        square = i * i\n        if num1 <= square <= num2:\n            result_list.append(square)\n\n    return result_list\n```\n"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/589", "solution": "```python\nimport math\n\ndef perfect_squares(lower_bound: int, upper_bound: int) -> list[int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Identifies and returns all perfect squares within a given inclusive integer range.\n    Uses square root calculation for efficient finding of perfect squares.\n    \"\"\"\n    result = []\n    # Perfect squares are non-negative, so adjust lower_bound if it's negative.\n    effective_lower_bound = max(0, lower_bound)\n\n    # Calculate the integer square roots of the bounds.\n    start_sqrt = math.ceil(math.sqrt(effective_lower_bound))\n    end_sqrt = math.floor(math.sqrt(upper_bound))\n\n    # Iterate through potential integer square roots.\n    for i in range(start_sqrt, end_sqrt + 1):\n        square = i * i\n        result.append(square)\n\n    return result\n```\n"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/592", "solution": "```python\nimport math\n\ndef sum_Of_product(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the sum of the product of consecutive binomial coefficients C(n, k) * C(n, k+1).\n    The sum is computed for k ranging from 0 to n-1 using math.comb.\n    \"\"\"\n    total_sum = 0\n    for k in range(n):\n        C_nk = math.comb(n, k)\n        C_nk_plus_1 = math.comb(n, k + 1)\n\n        product = C_nk * C_nk_plus_1\n        total_sum += product\n    return total_sum\n```\n"}
