{"task_id": "Mbpp/592", "solution": "def _factorial(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the factorial of a non-negative integer n.\n    Returns 1 for n=0.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 1\n    result = 1\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        result *= i\n    return result\n\ndef _binomial_coefficient(n: int, k: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the binomial coefficient C(n, k).\n    Returns 0 if k is out of bounds (k < 0 or k > n).\n    \"\"\"\n    if k < 0 or k > n:\n        return 0\n    # C(n, k) = n! / (k! * (n-k)!)\n    return _factorial(n) // (_factorial(k) * _factorial(n - k))\n\ndef sum_Of_product(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the sum of products of consecutive binomial coefficients.\n    The sum is C(n,0)*C(n,1) + C(n,1)*C(n,2) + ... + C(n,n-1)*C(n,n).\n    \"\"\"\n    total_sum = 0\n    for k in range(n):  # Iterate from k=0 to n-1\n        coeff1 = _binomial_coefficient(n, k)\n        coeff2 = _binomial_coefficient(n, k + 1)\n        total_sum += coeff1 * coeff2\n    return total_sum"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/593", "solution": "```python\ndef removezero_ip(ip_address_str: str) -> str:\n    # Splits the IP address into octets, processes each to remove leading zeros, and reconstructs it.\n    octets = ip_address_str.split('.')\n    normalized_octets = []\n    for octet in octets:\n        # Convert to int to remove leading zeros, then back to string.\n        normalized_octets.append(str(int(octet)))\n    return '.'.join(normalized_octets)\n```"}
