{"task_id": "Mbpp/598", "solution": "```python\ndef armstrong_number(number: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if a given integer is an Armstrong number.\n    An Armstrong number is one whose sum of digits raised to the power of the number of digits equals the original number.\"\"\"\n\n    # Convert the number to a string to find the count of its digits.\n    num_str = str(number)\n    num_digits = len(num_str)\n\n    sum_of_powers = 0\n    temporary_number = number\n\n    # Extract each digit, raise it to the power of num_digits, and add to the sum.\n    while temporary_number > 0:\n        digit = temporary_number % 10\n        sum_of_powers += digit ** num_digits\n        temporary_number //= 10\n\n    return sum_of_powers == number\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/597", "solution": "```python\ndef find_kth(arr1: list, arr2: list, k: int) -> any:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the kth element from two combined sorted arrays.\n    Assumes arr1 and arr2 are sorted, and k is a valid 1-based index.\n    \"\"\"\n    ptr1 = 0\n    ptr2 = 0\n\n    while k > 0:\n        if ptr1 == len(arr1):\n            return arr2[ptr2 + k - 1]\n        if ptr2 == len(arr2):\n            return arr1[ptr1 + k - 1]\n\n        if k == 1:\n            return min(arr1[ptr1], arr2[ptr2])\n\n        if arr1[ptr1] <= arr2[ptr2]:\n            ptr1 += 1\n        else:\n            ptr2 += 1\n\n        k -= 1\n\n```"}
