{"task_id": "Mbpp/603", "solution": "```python\ndef get_ludic(n: int) -> list[int]:\n    \"\"\"Calculates ludic numbers up to n using a sieve-like algorithm.\"\"\"\n    if n < 1:\n        return []\n\n    ludic_numbers = []\n    remaining_numbers = list(range(1, n + 1))\n\n    while remaining_numbers:\n        current_ludic = remaining_numbers[0]\n        ludic_numbers.append(current_ludic)\n\n        if current_ludic == 1:\n            remaining_numbers.pop(0)\n        else:\n            next_remaining = []\n            count = 0\n            # Iterate through numbers after current_ludic in the remaining_numbers list\n            # and sieve based on count % current_ludic.\n            for x in remaining_numbers[1:]:\n                count += 1\n                if count % current_ludic != 0:\n                    next_remaining.append(x)\n            remaining_numbers = next_remaining\n\n    return ludic_numbers\n```"}
