{"task_id": "Mbpp/607", "solution": "```python\ndef find_literals(text: str, pattern: str) -> tuple[str, int, int]:\n    # Searches 'text' for the first occurrence of 'pattern'.\n    # Returns (matched_substring, start_index, end_index) or (None, -1, -1) if no match.\n    import re\n    match = re.search(pattern, text)\n    if match:\n        return (match.group(0), match.start(), match.end())\n    else:\n        return (None, -1, -1)\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/607", "solution": "```python\nimport re\n\ndef find_literals(target_string: str, regex_pattern: str) -> tuple[str, int, int] | None:\n    \"\"\"\n    Searches a string for a regex pattern and returns matching details.\n    Returns None if no match is found or the pattern is invalid.\n    \"\"\"\n    try:\n        # Compile the regex pattern for efficiency and to catch invalid patterns.\n        compiled_pattern = re.compile(regex_pattern)\n    except re.error:\n        # Return None for invalid regex patterns.\n        return None\n\n    # Search for the pattern in the target string.\n    match = compiled_pattern.search(target_string)\n\n    if match:\n        # Return the matching substring, its start and end indices.\n        return (match.group(0), match.start(), match.end())\n    else:\n        # Return None if no match is found.\n        return None\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/608", "solution": "```python\ndef bell_Number(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the nth Bell number using dynamic programming (Bell triangle method).\"\"\"\n    # Initialize a 2D list for the Bell triangle.\n    bell = [[0] * (n + 1) for _ in range(n + 1)]\n\n    # Base case: B_0 = 1\n    bell[0][0] = 1\n\n    # Fill the Bell triangle\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        # The first element of row i is the last element of row i-1\n        bell[i][0] = bell[i - 1][i - 1]\n        for j in range(1, i + 1):\n            # Other elements are the sum of the element above and the element to its left\n            bell[i][j] = bell[i - 1][j - 1] + bell[i][j - 1]\n\n    # The nth Bell number is the first element of the nth row (bell[n][0])\n    return bell[n][0]\n```\n"}
