{"task_id": "Mbpp/608", "solution": "```python\ndef bell_Number(n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the nth Bell number using dynamic programming (Bell triangle).\n    The Bell numbers count the number of partitions of a set with n elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(n, int):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input 'n' must be an integer.\")\n    if n < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input 'n' must be a non-negative integer.\")\n    if n == 0:\n        return 1\n\n    # Initialize the first row of the Bell triangle (B_0)\n    bell_row = [1]\n\n    # Build the Bell triangle row by row up to n\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        # The first element of the new row is the last element of the previous row\n        new_row = [bell_row[-1]]\n        # Calculate subsequent elements in the new row\n        for j in range(1, i + 1):\n            new_row.append(new_row[j - 1] + bell_row[j - 1])\n        bell_row = new_row\n\n    # The nth Bell number is the first element of the nth row\n    return bell_row[0]\n```\n"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/616", "solution": "```python\ndef tuple_modulo(tuple1, tuple2):\n    \"\"\"Performs element-wise modulo operations on two input tuples.\n    Tuples must be of the same length; otherwise, a ValueError is raised.\"\"\"\n    if len(tuple1) != len(tuple2):\n        raise ValueError(\"Tuples must have the same length\")\n\n    results = [tuple1[i] % tuple2[i] for i in range(len(tuple1))]\n    return tuple(results)\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/616", "solution": "```python\ndef tuple_modulo(tuple1, tuple2):\n    \"\"\"Performs an element-wise modulo operation on two input tuples.\n    Returns a new tuple containing the results.\"\"\"\n    results = [element1 % element2 for element1, element2 in zip(tuple1, tuple2)]\n    return tuple(results)\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/620", "solution": "```python\ndef largest_subset(numbers):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the size of the largest subset of numbers where every pair is divisible.\n    This uses dynamic programming after sorting the input list.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not numbers:\n        return 0\n\n    numbers.sort()\n    n = len(numbers)\n    dp = [1] * n  # dp[i] stores the size of the largest divisible subset ending with numbers[i]\n    max_size = 1\n\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(i):\n            if numbers[i] % numbers[j] == 0:\n                dp[i] = max(dp[i], dp[j] + 1)\n        max_size = max(max_size, dp[i])\n\n    return max_size\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/618", "solution": "```python\ndef div_list(list1: list[float | int], list2: list[float | int]) -> list[float]:\n    \"\"\"Divides each element of list1 by the corresponding element of list2. Returns a new list of floating-point results, truncated to the length of the shorter input list.\"\"\"\n    result = []\n    for i in range(min(len(list1), len(list2))):\\\n        result.append(float(list1[i]) / list2[i])\n    return result\n```"}
