{"task_id": "Mbpp/620", "solution": "```python\ndef largest_subset(list_of_numbers: list[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the size of the largest divisible subset from a list of numbers.\n    A divisible subset means every pair (x, y) within it satisfies x % y == 0 or y % x == 0.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(list_of_numbers)\n\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n\n    # Sort the input list to simplify divisibility checks.\n    nums = sorted(list_of_numbers)\n\n    # dp[i] stores the size of the largest divisible subset ending with nums[i].\n    dp = [1] * n\n    max_size = 1\n\n    # Iterate through each number to build up the largest divisible subsets.\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(i):\n            if nums[i] % nums[j] == 0:\n                dp[i] = max(dp[i], dp[j] + 1)\n        max_size = max(max_size, dp[i])\n\n    return max_size\n```"}
