{"task_id": "Mbpp/622", "solution": "```python\ndef get_median(list1: list[int], list2: list[int], size: int) -> float:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the median of two sorted lists of the same size.\n    It uses a two-pointer approach to find the two middle elements in O(n) time.\n    \"\"\"\n    i = 0\n    j = 0\n    m1 = 0  # Stores the (size)-th element of the combined sorted list\n    m2 = 0  # Stores the (size+1)-th element of the combined sorted list\n\n    # Iterate size + 1 times to find the two middle elements needed for the median.\n    for _ in range(size + 1):\n        m1 = m2  # m1 holds the previous m2 value\n\n        if i == size:  # If list1 is exhausted, take from list2\n            m2 = list2[j]\n            j += 1\n        elif j == size:  # If list2 is exhausted, take from list1\n            m2 = list1[i]\n            i += 1\n        elif list1[i] < list2[j]:  # Current element in list1 is smaller\n            m2 = list1[i]\n            i += 1\n        else:  # Current element in list2 is smaller or equal\n            m2 = list2[j]\n            j += 1\n\n    return (m1 + m2) / 2.0\n\n```\n"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/622", "solution": "```python\ndef get_median(list1: list[float | int], list2: list[float | int], size: int) -> float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the median of two combined sorted lists of the same size.\n    Assumes input lists are sorted and of the same size.\n    \"\"\"\n    idx1 = 0\n    idx2 = 0\n    median_val1 = 0\n    median_val2 = 0\n\n    # Iterate to find the two middle elements without a full merge.\n    # The loop runs 'size + 1' times to find the element at conceptual index 'size' and 'size - 1'.\n    for k in range(size + 1):\n        if idx1 == size:\n            median_val1 = median_val2\n            median_val2 = list2[idx2]\n            idx2 += 1\n        elif idx2 == size:\n            median_val1 = median_val2\n            median_val2 = list1[idx1]\n            idx1 += 1\n        elif list1[idx1] <= list2[idx2]:\n            median_val1 = median_val2\n            median_val2 = list1[idx1]\n            idx1 += 1\n        else:\n            median_val1 = median_val2\n            median_val2 = list2[idx2]\n            idx2 += 1\n\n    return float(median_val1 + median_val2) / 2.0\n```"}
