{"task_id": "Mbpp/635", "solution": "```python\ndef heap_sort(arr: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Sorts a list in ascending order using the heap sort algorithm.\n    The sorting is performed in-place.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(arr)\n\n    # Build a maxheap.\n    # The loop goes from the last non-leaf node up to the root.\n    for i in range(n // 2 - 1, -1, -1):\n        _heapify(arr, n, i)\n\n    # Extract elements one by one\n    # The loop goes from the last element down to the second element.\n    for i in range(n - 1, 0, -1):\n        # Swap current root with current last element\n        arr[i], arr[0] = arr[0], arr[i]\n        # Call _heapify on the reduced heap (size i)\n        _heapify(arr, i, 0)\n\n    return arr\n\ndef _heapify(arr: list, n: int, i: int) -> None:\n    \"\"\"\n    Maintains the max-heap property for a subtree rooted at index i.\n    It assumes subtrees rooted at left and right children are already heapified.\n    \"\"\"\n    largest = i  # Initialize largest as root\n    left_child = 2 * i + 1\n    right_child = 2 * i + 2\n\n    # See if left child of root exists and is greater than root\n    if left_child < n and arr[largest] < arr[left_child]:\n        largest = left_child\n\n    # See if right child of root exists and is greater than current largest\n    if right_child < n and arr[largest] < arr[right_child]:\n        largest = right_child\n\n    # Change root, if needed\n    if largest != i:\n        arr[i], arr[largest] = arr[largest], arr[i]  # swap\n        # Heapify the root.\n        _heapify(arr, n, largest)\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/635", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List, TypeVar, Any\n\nComparable = TypeVar('Comparable', bound='_Comparable')\n\nclass _Comparable:\n    def __lt__(self, other: Any) -> bool: ...\n    def __gt__(self, other: Any) -> bool: ...\n    def __eq__(self, other: Any) -> bool: ...\n\ndef _heapify(arr: List[Comparable], n: int, i: int) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Maintains the max-heap property for a subtree rooted at index i.\"\"\"\n    # Finds the largest element among the root, left child, and right child.\n    largest = i\n    left = 2 * i + 1\n    right = 2 * i + 2\n\n    if left < n and arr[left] > arr[largest]:\n        largest = left\n\n    if right < n and arr[right] > arr[largest]:\n        largest = right\n\n    if largest != i:\n        arr[i], arr[largest] = arr[largest], arr[i]  # Swap\n        _heapify(arr, n, largest)  # Recursively heapify the affected sub-tree\n\ndef _build_max_heap(arr: List[Comparable]) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Builds a max-heap from an unsorted array.\"\"\"\n    # Arranges elements in arr such that the max-heap property is satisfied for all nodes.\n    n = len(arr)\n    # Start from the last non-leaf node and heapify upwards.\n    for i in range(n // 2 - 1, -1, -1):\n        _heapify(arr, n, i)\n\ndef heap_sort(input_list: List[Comparable]) -> List[Comparable]:\n    \"\"\"Sorts a list using the heap sort algorithm.\"\"\"\n    # Creates a mutable copy to avoid modifying the original list in place.\n    arr = list(input_list)\n    n = len(arr)\n\n    # First, build a max-heap from the input array.\n    _build_max_heap(arr)\n\n    # Extract elements one by one from the heap to sort the array.\n    for i in range(n - 1, 0, -1):\n        arr[i], arr[0] = arr[0], arr[i]  # Swap current root with last element\n        _heapify(arr, i, 0)  # Heapify the reduced heap\n\n    return arr\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/633", "solution": "```python\ndef pair_xor_Sum(numbers: list[int], n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the sum of bitwise XORs for all unique pairs in the given list.\"\"\"\n    total_xor_sum = 0\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(i + 1, n):\n            pair_xor = numbers[i] ^ numbers[j]\n            total_xor_sum += pair_xor\n    return total_xor_sum\n```"}
