{"task_id": "Mbpp/638", "solution": "```python\ndef wind_chill(velocity_kmh: float, temperature_celsius: float) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the wind chill index rounded to the nearest integer given the wind velocity in km/h and a temperature in celsius.\n\n    The Canadian Wind Chill Index formula is used:\n    WCI = 13.12 + 0.6215 * T - 11.37 * V^0.16 + 0.3965 * T * V^0.16\n    Where:\n    T is temperature_celsius\n    V is velocity_kmh\n\n    The result is rounded to the nearest integer to match the provided assert example.\n\n    Args:\n        velocity_kmh (float): The wind velocity in kilometers per hour.\n        temperature_celsius (float): The ambient temperature in Celsius.\n\n    Returns:\n        int: The calculated wind chill index, rounded to the nearest integer.\n    \"\"\"\n    T = temperature_celsius\n    V = velocity_kmh\n\n    # Calculate V^0.16\n    V_power_16 = V**0.16\n\n    # Apply the Canadian Wind Chill Index formula\n    raw_wci = 13.12 + (0.6215 * T) - (11.37 * V_power_16) + (0.3965 * T * V_power_16)\n\n    # Round to the nearest integer to match the provided assert example: wind_chill(120,35) == 40\n    return round(raw_wci)\n```"}
