{"task_id": "Mbpp/644", "solution": "```python\ndef reverse_Array_Upto_K(arr: list, k: int) -> list:\n    \"\"\"Reverses the first k elements of an array in-place.\n    Assumes k is a valid non-negative index within array bounds.\"\"\"\n    left = 0\n    right = k - 1\n\n    while left < right:\n        arr[left], arr[right] = arr[right], arr[left]\n        left += 1\n        right -= 1\n    return arr\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/644", "solution": "```python\ndef reverse_Array_Upto_K(array: list, k: int) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Reverses the order of the first 'k' elements of the input array.\n    The function modifies the initial part of the array based on 'k'.\n    \"\"\"\n    effective_k = max(0, min(k, len(array)))\n\n    reversed_part = array[:effective_k][::-1]\n\n    return reversed_part + array[effective_k:]\n```"}
