{"task_id": "Mbpp/733", "solution": "```python\ndef find_first_occurrence(sorted_array: list[int | float], target_number: int | float) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Locates the 0-based index of the first occurrence of a target number in a sorted array.\n    Returns -1 if the target number is not found.\n    \"\"\"\n    low = 0\n    high = len(sorted_array) - 1\n    result = -1\n\n    while low <= high:\n        mid = low + (high - low) // 2\n        if sorted_array[mid] == target_number:\n            result = mid\n            high = mid - 1  # Try to find an earlier occurrence in the left half\n        elif sorted_array[mid] < target_number:\n            low = mid + 1\n        else:  # sorted_array[mid] > target_number\n            high = mid - 1\n    return result\n```"}
