{"task_id": "Mbpp/735", "solution": "```python\ndef toggle_middle_bits(number: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Toggles all bits of the input integer except its most significant bit (MSB) and least significant bit (LSB).\n    Returns the modified integer.\n    \"\"\"\n    bit_length = number.bit_length()\n\n    # If the number has 2 or fewer bits, there are no middle bits to toggle.\n    if bit_length <= 2:\n        return number\n\n    # Create a mask for all bits required to represent the number.\n    full_mask = (1 << bit_length) - 1\n\n    # Create a mask to isolate the MSB position.\n    msb_mask = 1 << (bit_length - 1)\n\n    # Create a mask to isolate the LSB position.\n    lsb_mask = 1\n\n    # The middle_mask has 1s at all positions except the MSB and LSB.\n    middle_mask = full_mask ^ msb_mask ^ lsb_mask\n\n    # Toggle the middle bits using XOR; MSB and LSB positions remain unchanged.\n    result = number ^ middle_mask\n\n    return result\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/735", "solution": "```python\ndef toggle_middle_bits(number: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Toggles all bits of an integer except the most significant (first) and least significant (last).\"\"\"\n\n    # Convert the number to its binary string representation, removing the '0b' prefix.\n    binary_str = bin(number)[2:]\n    num_bits = len(binary_str)\n\n    # If the number has 0, 1, or 2 bits, no intermediate bits exist to toggle.\n    if num_bits <= 2:\n        return number\n\n    # Extract the most significant bit, least significant bit, and intermediate bits.\n    msb = binary_str[0]\n    lsb = binary_str[-1]\n    intermediate_bits = binary_str[1:-1]\n\n    # Toggle each intermediate bit.\n    toggled_intermediate_bits = \"\"\n    for bit in intermediate_bits:\n        toggled_intermediate_bits += '1' if bit == '0' else '0'\n\n    # Reconstruct the new binary string and convert it back to an integer.\n    new_binary_str = msb + toggled_intermediate_bits + lsb\n    return int(new_binary_str, 2)\n```\n"}
