{"task_id": "Mbpp/739", "solution": "```python\ndef find_Index(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Finds the index k of the smallest triangular number T_k with n digits.\n    T_k has n digits if 10^(n-1) <= T_k < 10^n.\n    \"\"\"\n    lower_bound = 10**(n - 1) # Calculate the lower bound for an n-digit number.\n    upper_bound = 10**n # Calculate the upper bound for an n-digit number.\n\n    k = 1 # Start searching for k from 1.\n\n    while True:\n        t_k = k * (k + 1) // 2 # Calculate the triangular number T_k.\n\n        if t_k >= lower_bound and t_k < upper_bound: # Check if T_k has exactly 'n' digits.\n            return k # Return k if condition met.\n\n        k += 1\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/739", "solution": "```python\nimport math\n\ndef _calculate_triangular_number_value(k: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the k-th triangular number.\n    It uses the formula k * (k + 1) / 2.\"\"\"\n    return k * (k + 1) // 2\n\ndef _count_digits(number: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Determines the number of digits of a positive integer.\n    It uses a logarithmic calculation.\"\"\"\n    return math.floor(math.log10(number)) + 1\n\ndef find_Index(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Finds the index k of the smallest triangular number with exactly n digits.\n    It iteratively calculates triangular numbers until the digit count matches n.\"\"\"\n    k = 1\n    while True:\n        triangular_value = _calculate_triangular_number_value(k)\n        num_digits = _count_digits(triangular_value)\n        if num_digits == n:\n            return k\n        k += 1\n```"}
