{"task_id": "Mbpp/740", "solution": "```python\ndef tuple_to_dict(input_tuple: tuple) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"\n    Converts a tuple into a key-value dictionary where adjacent elements form pairs.\n    If the tuple has an odd number of elements, the last one is ignored.\n    \"\"\"\n    result_dict = {}\n    # Iterate with a step of 2 to get adjacent pairs\n    # Stop one element before the end to ensure a pair can always be formed\n    for i in range(0, len(input_tuple) - 1, 2):\n        key = input_tuple[i]\n        value = input_tuple[i+1]\n        result_dict[key] = value\n    return result_dict\n```"}
