{"task_id": "Mbpp/743", "solution": "```python\ndef rotate_right(input_list: list, num_rotations: int) -> list:\n    \"\"\"Rotates a list to the right by a specified number of items.\n    Returns a new list with the elements rotated, leaving the original list unchanged.\n    \"\"\"\n    list_length = len(input_list)\n\n    # Handle edge cases: empty list or zero effective rotations.\n    if list_length == 0:\n        return []\n\n    effective_rotations = num_rotations % list_length\n\n    # If effective rotations result in no change (e.g., num_rotations is a multiple of list_length),\n    # return a copy of the original list.\n    if effective_rotations == 0:\n        return list(input_list)\n\n    # Perform the rotation by slicing the list into two parts and concatenating them.\n    # The last 'effective_rotations' elements become the new prefix.\n    rotated_list = input_list[-effective_rotations:] + input_list[:-effective_rotations]\n\n    return rotated_list\n```"}
