{"task_id": "Mbpp/745", "solution": "```python\ndef _get_digits(number: int) -> list[int]:\n    \"\"\"Extracts individual digits from a number.\n    Converts the number to a string and then to a list of integers.\"\"\"\n    return [int(d) for d in str(number)]\n\ndef _is_divisible_by_all_non_zero_digits(number: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if a number is divisible by all its non-zero constituent digits.\n    Ignores the digit '0' in divisibility checks.\"\"\"\n    digits = _get_digits(number)\n    for digit in digits:\n        if digit == 0:\n            continue\n        if number % digit != 0:\n            return False\n    return True\n\ndef divisible_by_digits(startnum: int, endnum: int) -> list[int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds numbers within a given range (inclusive) that are divisible by all their non-zero digits.\n    It iterates through each number and uses helper functions for digit extraction and divisibility checks.\n    \"\"\"\n    result_list = []\n    for number in range(startnum, endnum + 1):\n        if _is_divisible_by_all_non_zero_digits(number):\n            result_list.append(number)\n    return result_list\n```"}
