{"task_id": "Mbpp/751", "solution": "```python\ndef check_min_heap(arr):\n    \"\"\"Checks if the given array represents a min-heap.\n    It verifies the min-heap property for all parent nodes.\"\"\"\n    n = len(arr)\n    # An empty or single-element array is always a min-heap.\n    # The loop for parent nodes will not execute for n < 2, correctly returning True.\n    for i in range(n // 2):\n        left_child_idx = 2 * i + 1\n        right_child_idx = 2 * i + 2\n\n        # Check left child\n        if left_child_idx < n and arr[left_child_idx] < arr[i]:\n            return False\n\n        # Check right child\n        if right_child_idx < n and arr[right_child_idx] < arr[i]:\n            return False\n\n    return True\n```"}
