{"task_id": "Mbpp/751", "solution": "```python\ndef check_min_heap(array: list) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if the given array represents a valid min heap.\n    It iterates through potential parent nodes and compares them with their children.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(array)\n\n    if n <= 1:\n        return True\n\n    # Iterate only through nodes that can be parents\n    # The last potential parent node is at index (n // 2) - 1\n    for parent_index in range(n // 2):\n        left_child_index = 2 * parent_index + 1\n        right_child_index = 2 * parent_index + 2\n\n        # Check left child\n        if left_child_index < n:\n            if array[parent_index] > array[left_child_index]:\n                return False\n\n        # Check right child\n        if right_child_index < n:\n            if array[parent_index] > array[right_child_index]:\n                return False\n\n    return True\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/752", "solution": "```python\ndef jacobsthal_num(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the nth Jacobsthal number.\n    Uses the recurrence J(n) = J(n-1) + 2 * J(n-2) with J(0)=0 and J(1)=1.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n    if n == 1:\n        return 1\n\n    # Initialize for J(0) and J(1)\n    a, b = 0, 1\n\n    # Calculate iteratively for n > 1\n    for _ in range(2, n + 1):\n        next_val = b + 2 * a\n        a = b\n        b = next_val\n    return b\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/752", "solution": "```python\ndef jacobsthal_num(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the nth Jacobsthal number iteratively.\n    Uses the recurrence J(n) = J(n-1) + 2 * J(n-2) with base cases J(0)=0 and J(1)=1.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n    if n == 1:\n        return 1\n\n    # Initialize with J(0) and J(1)\n    a, b = 0, 1\n    # Iterate from J(2) up to J(n)\n    for _ in range(2, n + 1):\\\n        current_jacobsthal = b + 2 * a\n        a = b\n        b = current_jacobsthal\n    return b\n```"}
