{"task_id": "Mbpp/757", "solution": "```python\ndef count_reverse_pairs(string_list: list[str]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts unique reverse string pairs in the provided list.\n    A pair (s1, s2) is counted if s1 is the reverse of s2, and they are distinct strings.\n    \"\"\"\n    def _reverse_string(s: str) -> str:\n        \"\"\"Reverses a single input string.\"\"\"\n        return s[::-1]\n\n    pair_count = 0\n    seen_strings = set()\n    input_set = set(string_list)\n\n    for string in string_list:\n        if string in seen_strings:\n            continue\n\n        reversed_string = _reverse_string(string)\n\n        if reversed_string in input_set and string != reversed_string and reversed_string not in seen_strings:\n            pair_count += 1\n            seen_strings.add(string)\n            seen_strings.add(reversed_string)\n        else:\n            # Mark the current string as seen to prevent reprocessing it in the outer loop.\n            seen_strings.add(string)\n\n    return pair_count\n```\n"}
