{"task_id": "Mbpp/765", "solution": "```python\ndef is_polite(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the nth polite number.\n    A polite number is a positive integer that is not a power of 2.\n    \"\"\"\n    count = 0\n    num = 0\n    while count < n:\n        num += 1\n        # Check if the current number 'num' is a power of 2.\n        # A positive integer is a power of 2 if and only if it has exactly one bit set to 1.\n        # This can be efficiently checked using the bitwise operation: num > 0 and (num & (num - 1) == 0).\n        is_power_of_two = (num > 0 and (num & (num - 1) == 0))\n\n        if not is_power_of_two:\n            count += 1\n            if count == n:\n                return num\n\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/765", "solution": "```python\ndef is_polite(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the nth polite number, defined as the nth positive integer that is not a power of 2.\n    For example, the 7th polite number is 11.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n <= 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"n must be a positive integer.\")\n\n    count = 0\n    num = 0\n    while count < n:\n        num += 1\n        # Check if num is NOT a power of 2.\n        # A number is a power of 2 if (num > 0) and (num & (num - 1) == 0).\n        if not (num > 0 and (num & (num - 1) == 0)):\n            count += 1\n    return num\n```"}
