{"task_id": "Mbpp/771", "solution": "```python\ndef check_expression(expression: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if the given expression has balanced and correctly nested parentheses, square brackets, and curly braces.\n    It uses a stack-based approach to track opening brackets and validate their closure.\n    \"\"\"\n    stack = []\n    bracket_map = {\n        '(': ')',\n        '[': ']',\n        '{': '}'\n    }\n    opening_brackets = set(bracket_map.keys())\n    closing_brackets = set(bracket_map.values())\n\n    for char in expression:\n        if char in opening_brackets:\n            stack.append(char)\n        elif char in closing_brackets:\n            if not stack:\n                return False\n\n            last_open = stack.pop()\n            if bracket_map[last_open] != char:\n                return False\n\n    return not stack\n```"}
