{"task_id": "Mbpp/781", "solution": "```python\nimport math\n\ndef count_divisors(n: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if the total count of divisors for an integer n is an even number.\n    Returns True if the divisor count is even, False otherwise.\n    \"\"\"\n    count = 0\n    # Iterate from 1 up to the square root of n to find divisors efficiently.\n    for i in range(1, int(math.sqrt(n)) + 1):\n        if n % i == 0:\n            # If i*i == n, i is a perfect square root, so count it once.\n            if i * i == n:\n                count += 1\n            # Otherwise, i and n/i are distinct divisors, so count both.\n            else:\n                count += 2\n    return count % 2 == 0\n```"}
