{"task_id": "Mbpp/780", "solution": "```python\ndef find_combinations(tuple_list: list[tuple]) -> list[tuple]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes element-wise sums of unique tuple pairs from the input list.\n    Pairs are generated by combining each element with all subsequent elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    results_list = []\n    n = len(tuple_list)\n\n    for i in range(n):\n        tuple1 = tuple_list[i]\n        for j in range(i + 1, n):\n            tuple2 = tuple_list[j]\n            # Perform element-wise summation\n            sum_value0 = tuple1[0] + tuple2[0]\n            sum_value1 = tuple1[1] + tuple2[1]\n            new_tuple = (sum_value0, sum_value1)\n            results_list.append(new_tuple)\n\n    return results_list\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/781", "solution": "```python\ndef count_divisors(number: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if the total count of divisors for a given integer is an even number.\n    Returns True if the count is even, False if the count is odd.\n    \"\"\"\n    # A number has an odd count of divisors if and only if it is a perfect square.\n    # Therefore, we return True if the number is not a perfect square (even count).\n\n    # Calculate the integer square root of the number.\n    sqrt_num = int(number**0.5)\n\n    # Return True if the number is not a perfect square, otherwise False.\n    return sqrt_num * sqrt_num != number\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/782", "solution": "```python\ndef odd_length_sum(arr: list[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the total sum of all odd-length subarrays in the input array.\n    Iterates through all possible subarrays, summing elements of those with odd lengths.\"\"\"\n    total_sum = 0\n    n = len(arr)\n\n    for start_index in range(n):\n        for end_index in range(start_index, n):\n            subarray = arr[start_index : end_index + 1]\n            length = len(subarray)\n\n            if length % 2 != 0:\n                current_subarray_sum = sum(subarray)\n                total_sum += current_subarray_sum\n\n    return total_sum\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/769", "solution": "```python\ndef Diff(list1: list, list2: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the difference between two lists, returning elements from list1 not in list2.\n    Elements are ordered by original even indices first, then odd indices, preserving relative order.\n    \"\"\"\n    list2_set = set(list2)\n    even_indexed_elements = []\n    odd_indexed_elements = []\n\n    for i, element in enumerate(list1):\n        if element not in list2_set:\n            if i % 2 == 0:\n                even_indexed_elements.append(element)\n            else:\n                odd_indexed_elements.append(element)\n\n    return even_indexed_elements + odd_indexed_elements\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/785", "solution": "```python\ndef tuple_str_int(tuple_string: str) -> tuple:\n    \"\"\"\n    Converts a string representation of a tuple of numbers into an actual Python tuple of integers.\n    This function processes the string by removing parentheses, splitting elements, and converting each to an integer.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Remove outer parentheses and strip any leading/trailing whitespace\n    cleaned_string = tuple_string[1:-1].strip()\n\n    # Handle an empty tuple string, e.g., \"()\"\n    if not cleaned_string:\n        return ()\n\n    # Split the cleaned string by comma to get individual number strings\n    number_strings = cleaned_string.split(',')\n\n    # Convert each number string to an integer\n    converted_integers = []\n    for num_str in number_strings:\n        converted_integers.append(int(num_str.strip()))\n\n    # Convert the list of integers into a tuple and return\n    return tuple(converted_integers)\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/784", "solution": "```python\ndef is_even(number: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Determines if a given number is even.\n    An even number is an integer divisible by 2.\n    \"\"\"\n    return number % 2 == 0\n\ndef is_odd(number: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Determines if a given number is odd.\n    An odd number is an integer not divisible by 2.\n    \"\"\"\n    return number % 2 != 0\n\ndef find_first_even(numbers: list[int]) -> int | None:\n    \"\"\"\n    Identifies the first even number encountered in the input list.\n    It returns None if no even number is found.\n    \"\"\"\n    for number in numbers:\n        if is_even(number):\n            return number\n    return None\n\ndef find_first_odd(numbers: list[int]) -> int | None:\n    \"\"\"\n    Identifies the first odd number encountered in the input list.\n    It returns None if no odd number is found.\n    \"\"\"\n    for number in numbers:\n        if is_odd(number):\n            return number\n    return None\n\ndef mul_even_odd(numbers: list[int]) -> int | None:\n    \"\"\"\n    Accepts a list of numbers, identifies the first odd and first even numbers,\n    calculates their product, and returns the result. Returns None if either\n    the first odd or first even number is not found in the list.\n    \"\"\"\n    first_odd = find_first_odd(numbers)\n    first_even = find_first_even(numbers)\n\n    if first_odd is not None and first_even is not None:\n        return first_odd * first_even\n    else:\n        return None\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/785", "solution": "```python\ndef tuple_str_int(tuple_string: str) -> tuple[int, ...]:\n    \"\"\"Converts a string representation of a tuple into an integer tuple.\n    It trusts the caller's input to be a valid tuple string for integer conversion.\"\"\"\n    content = tuple_string.strip('()')\n\n    if not content:\n        return ()\n\n    elements_str = [e.strip() for e in content.split(',')]\n    integer_elements = tuple(int(e) for e in elements_str)\n\n    return integer_elements\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/784", "solution": "```python\ndef mul_even_odd(numbers: list) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the product of the first even and first odd number in a list.\n    Assumes the list contains both an even and an odd number.\n    \"\"\"\n    first_even = None\n    first_odd = None\n\n    for number in numbers:\n        if first_odd is None and number % 2 != 0:\n            first_odd = number\n\n        if first_even is None and number % 2 == 0:\n            first_even = number\n\n        if first_even is not None and first_odd is not None:\n            break\n\n    return first_odd * first_even\n```"}
