{"task_id": "Mbpp/786", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List, Union\n\ndef right_insertion(sorted_list: List[Union[int, float]], value: Union[int, float]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Locates the right insertion point for a value in a sorted list, ensuring O(log n) complexity.\n    It returns the index immediately following any existing occurrences of the value.\n    \"\"\"\n    low = 0\n    high = len(sorted_list)\n\n    while low < high:\n        mid = (low + high) // 2\n        if sorted_list[mid] <= value:\n            low = mid + 1\n        else:\n            high = mid\n    return low\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/786", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List, Any\n\ndef right_insertion(list: List[Any], value: Any) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Locates the right insertion point for a specified value in a sorted list.\n    It determines the index where 'value' should be inserted to maintain sorted order, immediately after any existing occurrences.\n    \"\"\"\n    low = 0\n    high = len(list)\n\n    while low < high:\n        mid = (low + high) // 2\n        if list[mid] <= value:\n            low = mid + 1\n        else:\n            high = mid\n    return low\n```"}
