{"task_id": "Mbpp/799", "solution": "```python\ndef left_rotate(n: int, d: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Performs a left bit rotation on a 32-bit integer n by d bits.\n\n    The rotation treats n as a 32-bit unsigned integer, and d is taken modulo 32.\n    \"\"\"\n    BITS = 32\n    MASK = 0xFFFFFFFF\n\n    # Normalize rotation amount and mask n to 32 bits.\n    d_eff = d % BITS\n    n_32bit = n & MASK\n\n    # Perform the rotation by combining left and right shifts, then mask to 32 bits.\n    return ((n_32bit << d_eff) | (n_32bit >> (BITS - d_eff))) & MASK\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/799", "solution": "```python\ndef left_rotate(number: int, d: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Rotates the bits of a 32-bit integer to the left by 'd' positions.\"\"\"\n    # Normalize the rotation amount to be within the range [0, 31].\n    shift_amount = d % 32\n    # Perform the left bit rotation, ensuring the result is constrained to 32 bits.\n    return ((number << shift_amount) & 0xFFFFFFFF) | (number >> (32 - shift_amount))\n```"}
