{"task_id": "Mbpp/803", "solution": "```python\ndef is_perfect_square(number: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Determines if a given integer is a perfect square.\n    Negative numbers are not considered perfect squares.\n    \"\"\"\n    if number < 0:\n        return False\n\n    # Calculate the integer part of the square root.\n    root_candidate = int(number ** 0.5)\n\n    # Check if squaring this integer root yields the original number.\n    return root_candidate * root_candidate == number\n```"}
