{"task_id": "Mbpp/805", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List, Union\n\ndef max_sum_list(list_of_lists: List[List[Union[int, float]]]) -> List[Union[int, float]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds and returns the inner list with the highest sum of its elements.\n    Handles negative numbers, floats, and returns the first encountered list in case of a tie.\n    \"\"\"\n    max_sum = float('-inf')\n    max_sum_list_item = None\n\n    for inner_list in list_of_lists:\n        current_sum = sum(inner_list)\n        if current_sum > max_sum:\n            max_sum = current_sum\n            max_sum_list_item = inner_list\n\n    return max_sum_list_item\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/793", "solution": "def last(arr: list, x: any) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Finds the last (highest) index of a target element in a sorted array. Returns -1 if the element is not found.\"\"\"\n    low = 0\n    high = len(arr) - 1\n    result = -1\n\n    while low <= high:\n        mid = (low + high) // 2\n        if arr[mid] == x:\n            result = mid\n            low = mid + 1  # Search in the right half for a later occurrence\n        elif arr[mid] < x:\n            low = mid + 1\n        else:  # arr[mid] > x\n            high = mid - 1\n    return result"}
